(function () {
  'use strict';
  const CAMPAIGNS = [{"id":"lumani-impact-mateo","slug":"mateo","title":"Mateo tiene 8 meses y lucha contra un cáncer en etapa cuatro","description":"El pequeño Mateo enfrenta una batalla que ningún niño debería vivir. Tiene solo 8 meses y ha sido diagnosticado con cáncer en etapa cuatro. Su mundo —y el de toda su familia— cambió de un día para otro.\n\nEn lugar de una infancia normal, llena de risas y descubrimientos, los días de Mateo transcurren en hospitales, rodeado de médicos, tratamientos y una incertidumbre constante.\n\nEl tratamiento oncológico requiere quimioterapia intensiva, medicamentos de alto costo, hospitalizaciones continuas y traslados a centros especializados. Cada sesión es un paso más en su lucha, pero también representa un enorme peso económico para su familia.\n\nLos médicos han programado nuevas fases del tratamiento. Para que puedan realizarse sin demoras, la familia necesita reunir los fondos a tiempo. Cada día que pasa sin recursos puede significar una interrupción en su recuperación.\n\nLa familia de Mateo no puede cubrir sola la quimioterapia, los medicamentos, los estudios clínicos, las hospitalizaciones y los traslados. Tu ayuda puede permitir que complete cada fase del tratamiento sin nuevas interrupciones.\n\nLa campaña original reportó 10.360.000 MXN recaudados de una meta de 18.500.000 MXN. Para esta presentación internacional, ambos valores fueron convertidos a dólares estadounidenses usando la tasa de referencia del Banco Central Europeo del 10 de septiembre de 2026.\n\nCualquier donación, aunque sea pequeña, puede acercar a Mateo al tratamiento completo que necesita. Si no puedes donar, compartir su historia también puede ayudar muchísimo.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/mateo/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/mateo/1.webp","uploads/campaigns/mateo/2.jpg","uploads/campaigns/mateo/3.webp","uploads/campaigns/mateo/4.jpg","uploads/campaigns/mateo/5.png"],"raised":611443,"goal":1091862,"currency":"USD","source_currency":"MXN","source_raised":10360000,"source_goal":18500000,"fx_rate_mxn_usd":0.05901959190309731,"fx_date":"2026-09-10","fx_source":"European Central Bank reference rates: 1 EUR = 19.6816 MXN and 1 EUR = 1.1616 USD","category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Familia de Mateo","location":"México","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"612","created_at":"2026-05-04T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://unidosporunacausa.online/mx/","alternate_source_url":"https://activesearch.site/mateo"},{"id":"8b58629c-326c-431e-a795-4aeec53a85ee","slug":"help-graceline-now","title":"Urgent Help Needed for Graceline's Second Bone Marrow Transplant","description":"My name is Gema. I am writing as a mother standing on the edge of losing everything our family holds dear. Our beautiful 12-year-old daughter, Graceline Famlevina, received the devastating news that her cancer has returned during her fifth cycle of maintenance chemotherapy.\n\nThe latest bone marrow aspiration results showed a 4.8% increase in leukemia cells. The previous Donor Lymphocyte Infusion and maintenance chemotherapy were unable to stop the aggressive growth. Her medical team says she must undergo two more cycles of intensive chemotherapy immediately, followed by a second bone marrow transplant.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-01.jpg|Graceline's medical journey\n\nIn less than one year, our little girl may have to endure two highly complex bone marrow transplants. We need to raise the cost of the second transplant while also living with the fear that her exhausted body may not survive it.\n\nThe Agony of Relapse\n\nOn May 20, 2026, Graceline began her first cycle of intensive chemotherapy after this heartbreaking relapse. Doctors placed a PICC line directly into her arm to administer the drugs needed to suppress the Acute Myeloid Leukemia cells. When the anesthesia wore off, the pain was sharp and overwhelming. Even the slightest touch near the line sent pain through her body.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-02.jpg|Graceline with her family\n\nWe pray that every stage of treatment goes smoothly and that she is given strength, patience, and moments of joy. She is incredibly tired, yet she continues to fight with everything she has because she knows she is our only remaining child.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-03.jpg|Graceline during treatment\n\nA Grief We Cannot Fully Mourn\n\nTwo years ago, while we were already fighting for Graceline through intensive chemotherapy, another tragedy shattered our family. Her younger brother Sean contracted meningitis. His illness moved so quickly that while we were trying to save our daughter, our son quietly slipped away from us. We buried our baby boy while Graceline was still fighting for her life in the hospital.\n\nThere is a particular silence in a home that has lost a child. We could not collapse or mourn Sean the way he deserved because Graceline still needed us. We dried our tears, put our masks back on, and returned to the oncology ward.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-04.jpg|Family moments with Graceline\n\nA Fleeting Victory\n\nFor a short time, we believed the cancer had been beaten. In April 2025, her symptoms returned with a sudden fever, a dangerously low platelet count, and rising blast cells. We rushed her to a hospital in Singapore, where doctors said she needed intensive chemotherapy followed by a bone marrow transplant.\n\nOn July 25, doctors told us her blast cells were negative and she was ready for transplant. In September 2025, Graceline completed her first bone marrow transplant. It was a tremendous victory, but that transplant alone cost approximately $300,000.\n\nAfter the critical 100-day milestone, she needed maintenance chemotherapy to prevent another relapse. The cost reached nearly $20,000 each month for medicine and blood tests. Her immune system remained dangerously weak, and the planned six maintenance cycles were eventually increased to eight.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-05.jpg|Hope during recovery\n\nBack to the Starting Line\n\nOn April 13, another bone marrow test brought the news we feared most: the cancer had returned. Most families worry about school grades and scraped knees. We worry about white blood cell counts, painful catheters, and invisible cancer cells in our daughter's blood.\n\nGraceline should be thinking about homework and friends. Instead, she faces chemotherapy side effects and the terrifying possibility of another transplant. I see the future she deserves, and I cannot let the same shadow that took Sean take her away too.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-06.jpg|Graceline needs urgent help\n\nWe Urgently Need Your Help\n\nTo save her life, doctors must perform intensive chemotherapy, a Donor Lymphocyte Infusion, and the second bone marrow transplant as soon as possible. The estimated total for this new phase is $363,700.\n\nWe have nothing left to sell and nowhere left to borrow from. We are humbly asking for help to cross this finish line. Every donation supports Graceline's immediate chemotherapy, medical care, and second transplant. Thank you for keeping our daughter in your prayers and standing with our family.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-07.jpg|Standing with Graceline\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-08.jpg|Graceline's fight continues\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-09.jpg|Please help Graceline","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/hero.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/hero.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-02.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-04.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-graceline-now/story-07.jpg"],"raised":377524.06,"goal":790000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Gema Listya","location":"Singapore","words_of_support":[{"name":"Anonymous","amount":"$99","time":"2 minutes ago","message":"Stay strong, Graceline. Praying for you."},{"name":"Sarah M.","amount":"$39","time":"8 minutes ago","message":"From one mother to another — holding you in my heart."},{"name":"James K.","amount":"$150","time":"14 minutes ago","message":"For the second transplant. You've got this."}],"donations_count":"5136","created_at":"2026-08-21T14:21:08+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://onehopefoundation.online/help-graceline-now/"},{"id":"help-save-fabi","slug":"help-save-fabi","title":"Make a donation to ease Fabi's severe pain and help save her life!","description":"Our family never imagined we would be writing words like these.\n\n \n\nRecently, our sister-in-law, Fabiane (Binha), was diagnosed with a rare type of glioblastoma, an aggressive and devastating form of brain cancer. This diagnosis has profoundly impacted her, her immediate family, and everyone who loves her. In a very short time, life has shifted into a new and uncertain reality.\n\n \n\nShe is a wife, a mom, a daughter, a sister, and someone who has always been willing to help, care for, and show up for others. Seeing someone so giving now facing such a difficult diagnosis is heartbreaking for all of us.\n\n \n\nShe is deeply loved by her family, who are standing beside her with strength and devotion. While not all of us can be physically present right now, this fundraiser is how our family can come together — to support her, to support those caring for her, and to ensure she has access to the care and resources she needs.\n\n \n\nThis journey requires immediate and specialized medical care, difficult decisions, and time — time away from work, from routine, and from normal life. Along with the emotional weight, the financial burden of treatments, possible travel, and daily expenses can quickly become overwhelming.\n\n \n\nWe created this fundraiser to help ease that burden, so our beloved sister-in-law and her family can focus on what matters most: treatment, comfort, hope, and being together.\n\n \n\nAny contribution, no matter the amount, will make a meaningful difference. If you are unable to donate, sharing this page or keeping her and our family in your thoughts and prayers is deeply appreciated.\n\n \n\nFrom our hearts, thank you for your kindness, compassion, and support during this incredibly difficult time.\n\n \n\nWith gratitude,\n\nOur Family","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/1.png","uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/2.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/3.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/4.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/5.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/6.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/help-save-fabi/7.jpeg"],"raised":273542,"goal":400000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Fabi Jhonson","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"20,9k","created_at":"2026-01-05T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-jazzy","slug":"jazzy","title":"Save Jazzy's life from brain cancer & being homeless","description":"Jazzy has been battling Neuroblastoma cancer for over 7 years. After years of treatments, surgeries, hospital stays, pain, and setbacks, her family is now desperately searching for the next option that could help save her life.\n\nJazzy’s cancer has now spread throughout her body, including her spine, arms, and brain. In the past two months alone, she has endured three major brain surgeries, had three tumors removed from her head, and doctors have recently found new bumps appearing across her body. She is also currently relearning how to walk.\n\nThey have spent every last penny they have to the point they are currently homeless.\n\nDespite everything she has been through, Jazzy is still fighting with so much strength, courage, and hope.\n\nRight now, Jazzy is running out of options, and her family is searching for clinical trials and specialized treatments that may give her another chance.\n\nHer family is doing everything possible to get her to a clinical trial and specialized treatment in Rome, Italy, along with any additional cancer treatments that could help save her life. The treatment starts at around $350,000 USD- a number they can only dream to achieve to possibly save her life.\n\nBecause of Jazzy’s extensive treatment needs, her family is currently unable to work. On top of medical costs and travel, they are also caring for their other children back home while trying to stay by Jazzy’s side through this fight.\n\nThe money raised will help Jazzy and her family with: Clinical trials and specialized cancer treatments Travel, lodging, gas, and food during out-of-state treatment\n\nPossible treatment opportunities in Rome, Italy (if we can raise enough)\n\nMedical expenses and additional care needed to fight her cancer Helping Jazzy and her family get out of homelessness\n\nSecuring a safe apartment and covering rent for as long as possible Supporting the family while they are unable to work during her treatment\n\nJazzy has been fighting for her life since she was a little girl. She has been through more than any child should ever have to face, but she is still here, still smiling, still hoping, and still fighting.\n\nPlease donate anything you can to help give Jazzy a chance at life-saving treatment, a safe home, and the support her family needs during this impossible time. If you cannot donate, please share this fundraiser. Sharing could help us reach the person, doctor, hospital, or supporter who can help change Jazzy’s life.\n\nThank you so much to everyone who loves, supports, prays for, and believes in Jazzy. Your kindness means more than words can ever explain.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/jazzy/103899599_1779234005640833_r-rplmicoip1ycmc2pbpq8czukv23cl8snk7h6qrb5qk.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/jazzy/103899599_1779234005640833_r-rplmicoip1ycmc2pbpq8czukv23cl8snk7h6qrb5qk.webp"],"raised":176542,"goal":200000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Jazzy","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jonathan Sherlock","amount":"$250","time":"21 hours","message":"Just made my donation. No child should ever have to go through something like this. I'm praying that you get the treatment you need and make a full recovery. Stay strong, Jazzy!"},{"name":"Jim Fulsher","amount":"$20","time":"1 day","message":"Donated and shared. I truly hope more people see this because every single contribution brings Jazzy one step closer to the treatment she desperately needs. We're all behind you!"},{"name":"Luciana Cardoso","amount":"$250","time":"4 days","message":"Your strength is absolutely incredible. I made my donation today and will continue praying for you and your family. Keep fighting, sweet girl—you have so many people cheering you on."},{"name":"Wilson Sants","amount":"$100","time":"6 days","message":"Just donated. We may not be able to take away everything she's been through, but together we can give her another chance. Please keep sharing and donating if you're able.🙏"},{"name":"Philip Ayers","amount":"$50","time":"6 days","message":"Every child deserves hope. My donation may be small, but when thousands of people come together, miracles can happen. Praying Jazzy gets the life-saving treatment she deserves. ❤️"},{"name":"United Lodge of Prudednce No.83","amount":"$100","time":"8 days","message":"Just donated. My heart breaks for everything Jazzy and her family have endured. I'm praying this campaign reaches the people who can help make her treatment possible. Stay strong, sweet girl!"},{"name":"Victoria Jones","amount":"$250","time":"2 months","message":"Donation sent. I can't imagine what your family is going through, but I hope this small contribution helps in some way. Wishing Jazzy strength, healing, and many brighter days ahead.\""},{"name":"Sophie Agnew","amount":"$50","time":"2 months","message":"I just gave what I could and shared this with my friends and family. Let's all come together to give Jazzy the chance she deserves. Every donation and every share truly matters."}],"donations_count":"6800","created_at":"2026-03-03T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/jazzy/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-teddy","slug":"help-teddy","title":"Help 5-year-old Teddy Beat Brain Cancer","description":"Hi, we're Cindy and Liam, and we're raising funds for our son, Teddy.\n\nJust a few months before his fifth birthday, Teddy was a happy little boy enjoying everything childhood should be about — playing, laughing and making memories with his family.\n\nNothing could have prepared us for how suddenly our lives were about to change.\n\nAfter becoming unwell, Teddy underwent a CT scan and we received the devastating news that he needed emergency brain surgery for a mass at the back of his brain.\n\nFollowing surgery, we were told every parent's worst nightmare.\n\nTeddy had metastatic medulloblastoma, a Grade 4 pediatric brain cancer with MYC amplification — one of the most aggressive forms of childhood brain cancer. By the time it was discovered, the disease had already spread throughout his brain, spine and cerebrospinal fluid.\n\nSince that day, our family has been living a reality we never imagined possible.\n\nTeddy has faced brain surgery, intensive treatment, countless hospital visits, scans, tests and procedures that no child should ever have to endure. Through every setback, he has continued to show a strength that inspires everyone around him.\n\nToday, we find ourselves facing the most important challenge of Teddy's journey so far. Despite everything he has been through, there is still hope.\n\nTeddy has been provisionally accepted into a pioneering clinical trial at Penn State Children's Hospital in Pennsylvania, USA. The trial uses DFMO therapy and has shown promising results in helping children with high-risk medulloblastoma remain in remission.\n\nFor the first time since Teddy's diagnosis, we have been given a genuine opportunity to fight for a future beyond this disease.\n\nBut there is one devastating obstacle: we have just 60 days to get Teddy to the United States and secure his place in the programme. After that, the opportunity may no longer be available to him.\n\nThe cost of treatment, medical monitoring, travel, accommodation and insurance is estimated to exceed $250,000 — far beyond what our family can raise alone.\n\nWe understand that no treatment comes with guarantees. But we cannot walk away from a chance that could help keep Teddy's cancer from returning. If Teddy's cancer relapses, his chances of survival become heartbreakingly low.\n\nThat is why we are asking for your help today.\n\nEvery donation will help give Teddy the opportunity to access this potentially life-saving treatment and the future every five-year-old deserves.\n\nIf you are unable to donate, sharing Teddy's story could be just as powerful and may help us reach someone who can.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read Teddy's story, for standing beside our family and for helping us fight for his future.\n\nWith love and gratitude,\nCindy, Liam and Teddy","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/1.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/1.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/2.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/3.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/4.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/5.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-teddy/6.jpg"],"raised":167842,"goal":250000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Cindy and Liam","location":"United Kingdom","words_of_support":[{"name":"Emily R.","amount":"","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Just donated. Sixty days isn't long, but hopefully together we can get Teddy to the USA in time. ❤️"},{"name":"Michael & Jennifer","amount":"","time":"2 hours ago","message":"My daughter was treated in America years ago. Please don't give up. Donated and shared."},{"name":"Daniel W.","amount":"$20","time":"1 day ago","message":"$20 donated. I hope thousands of others do the same. Let's get Teddy to Pennsylvania."}],"donations_count":"12500","created_at":"2026-07-14T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://hopefoundation.click/apps/pagefly?id=dfb8825f-8258-4be7-a0bc-ce7bfacf0fdf"},{"id":"help-emma","slug":"help-emma","title":"Support Emma Davis Fight Against Metastatic Melanoma","description":"My name is Emma Davis, and I am fighting metastatic melanoma — an advanced form of skin cancer that has spread beyond its original site and requires urgent, ongoing treatment.\n\nWhat began as a diagnosis none of us were prepared for has changed every part of my life. Treatment plans, hospital visits, medications, and the emotional weight of facing cancer have become my daily reality.\n\nMetastatic melanoma is aggressive. It demands specialized care, frequent monitoring, and access to treatments that are often expensive and not always fully covered. Alongside the physical battle, there is the financial strain — medical bills, travel to appointments, daily living costs, and the need to focus entirely on healing rather than worrying about how to pay for the next step.\n\nI am deeply grateful for the love and support of family and friends who have stood by me. This fundraiser exists because we cannot carry this burden alone — and because every act of kindness, no matter how small, brings hope and relief during one of the hardest chapters of my life.\n\nYour donation helps cover medical treatment, essential medications, living expenses during recovery, and the resources I need to keep fighting.\n\nIf you are unable to donate, sharing this page means more than you know. Thank you from the bottom of my heart for your compassion, your prayers, and your belief that better days are still possible.\n\nWith gratitude,\nEmma","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-emma/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-emma/1.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-emma/2.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-emma/3.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-emma/4.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-emma/5.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-emma/6.jpeg"],"raised":110816,"goal":120000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Emma Davis","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jane Cotta","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour","message":"God bless you and your family! You video touched my heart! Please stay strong and know people are praying for you and thinking of you everyday!"},{"name":"Julian Brown","amount":"$20","time":"12 hours","message":"Don't give up"},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"1 day","message":"In memory of my Husband Matthew who passed from cancer. Keep fighting and living each day - you get through it"},{"name":"William Gomes","amount":"$100","time":"4 days","message":"God is with you, we are with you, we'll keep you in our prayers❤️"},{"name":"Pamela Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"6 days","message":"A mother's strength is powerful—keep fighting, you're surrounded by love .God is with you every step covering you in strength and healing"},{"name":"Uilson Ramirez","amount":"$30","time":"8 days","message":"On behalf of our Worshipful Master, Steve Pallett, and all the Brethren of the Lodge, we wish you well"},{"name":"Vania Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"1 month","message":"God bless you"},{"name":"Uesley Miller","amount":"$50","time":"2 months","message":"We are praying for you, my friend, stay strong during this difficult time. We're in this together."}],"donations_count":"2,9k","created_at":"2026-02-12T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"b9b2ab37-114c-4f47-b766-00ca926563a6","slug":"help-daniel","title":"Help Daniel Get a Life-Saving Liver Transplant","description":"My name is Daniel, and in 2024 I was diagnosed with liver cancer.\n\nIt was not caused by an unhealthy lifestyle, but by a dormant hepatitis B infection that was passed from my mother to me at birth.\n\nI have been through multiple liver surgeries, chemotherapy, local treatments and fifteen cycles of immunotherapy. Unfortunately, despite all of these treatments, the cancer keeps coming back aggressively.\n\nToday, a living-donor liver transplant is my only chance of a cure. My latest scan showed a new aggressive tumour, but the good news is that there is no evidence the cancer has spread outside the liver. If it spreads beyond the liver, a transplant will no longer be an option and a cure may no longer be possible.\n\nThe transplant process in the Netherlands is taking longer than my doctors and I can safely afford because of how aggressively the cancer is recurring. I am sitting on a ticking time bomb and cannot wait until the process finally catches up with the urgency of my illness.\n\nAfter carefully reviewing every option with my medical team, I decided to move forward with the transplant process in Turkey. My hospital in the Netherlands is already working with Turkish doctors, and this route allows us to move much faster while the transplant is still clinically viable. Unfortunately, the treatment is not covered by my health insurance.\n\nAnyone who knows me knows that I have always believed that if something in my life needed fixing, it was my responsibility to find a solution. I never liked asking for help, especially when it came to money. I have come to realize that taking responsibility now does not mean trying to do everything alone. It means doing everything within my power to survive, even if that means setting my pride aside and asking for help.\n\nThe goal of this fundraiser is $114,000. The money will be used for:\n\n• Transplant surgery.\n\n• Donor surgery and medical evaluation.\n\n• Hospitalisation and medication.\n\n• Travel and accommodation.\n\n• Medical follow-up, recovery and a reserve for unexpected complications.\n\nThe donor does not receive any payment. The costs cover the donor's medical evaluation, surgery, hospitalisation and post-operative follow-up.\n\nEveryone who donates deserves full transparency. I will continue sharing updates throughout this process.\n\nIf you decide to donate, thank you. If donating is not possible, sharing this page with others can make an enormous difference.\n\nThank you for giving me a second chance at a wonderful life.\n\nWith love,\n\nDaniel","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-daniel/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-daniel/1.png","uploads/campaigns/help-daniel/2.png","uploads/campaigns/help-daniel/3.png","uploads/campaigns/help-daniel/4.png"],"raised":87803,"goal":114000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Daniel Mebius","location":"Netherlands","words_of_support":[{"name":"Emma Richardson","amount":"","time":"7 hours ago","message":"My dad had a liver transplant in 2019 and he's still here with us today. A living donor gave him that second chance. Praying you get yours in Turkey soon, Daniel. Don't lose hope."},{"name":"Jacob Hoffmann","amount":"","time":"1 day ago","message":"The fact that you kept fighting through fifteen rounds of immunotherapy says everything about the kind of man you are. Turkey is the right move if it means moving faster. Wishing you strength. 💚"},{"name":"Michael Brooks","amount":"","time":"2 days ago","message":"I don't know you, but I read your whole story and had to donate. Nobody should lose the chance at a transplant because the system moves too slowly. Sharing this everywhere I can."}],"donations_count":"12500","created_at":"2026-07-02T00:00:00+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://primehealth.org.uk/pages/help"},{"id":"help-vexanna","slug":"help-vexanna","title":"Help Save My Daughter Vexanna","description":"My name is Maria, and I am Vexanna's mother.\r\n\r\nI never imagined I would have to share my daughter's pain with the world to ask for help. As a mother, all I have ever wanted was to protect her. Today, I can no longer do it alone.\r\n\r\nVexanna was born with a rare condition called hydrocephalus, a disease that causes cerebrospinal fluid to build up inside the brain, creating dangerous pressure and causing her head to grow much larger than normal. From the day she was born, our lives became filled with hospitals, medical appointments, surgeries, fear, and uncertainty.\r\n\r\nWhen she was only 2 years old, our lives changed forever.\r\n\r\nOne night, while she was sleeping, the pressure inside her head became so severe that the fragile tissue covering her skull ruptured. I will never forget waking up to that nightmare.\r\n\r\nFluid from the wound began to leak, and before I realized what was happening, ants had entered our room and started crawling onto my baby's head. Seeing my little girl in that condition is something no mother should ever have to experience.\r\n\r\nThat moment broke my heart forever.\r\n\r\nSince that day, Vexanna has lived with an extremely fragile skull. Today, part of her head has little to no protective bone covering it. Instead of feeling hard like a normal skull, that area feels soft and incredibly delicate. Even the smallest bump or accidental touch could cause a devastating injury.\r\n\r\nWe live every single day in fear.\r\n\r\nHydrocephalus is much more than having an enlarged head. It can lead to seizures, severe headaches, vision loss, developmental delays, infections, mobility problems, and permanent brain damage if left untreated. Every day is a battle to keep my daughter safe.\r\n\r\nVexanna depends on me for absolutely everything.\r\n\r\nBecause of her condition, I cannot work. She needs constant supervision and care 24 hours a day. My days are spent taking her to medical appointments, giving her medications, caring for her delicate head, and doing everything I can to keep her alive.\r\n\r\nWhile I care for my daughter, our bills continue to grow.\r\n\r\nWe struggle to afford food, rent, electricity, transportation, medications, medical appointments, examinations, and the daily supplies she desperately needs.\r\n\r\nI never imagined I would have to ask strangers for help.\r\n\r\nBut when I look into my daughter's eyes and see her still smiling despite everything she has endured, I know I cannot give up.\r\n\r\nIf you can make a donation, no matter how small, you will be helping us continue Vexanna's treatment, provide the care she desperately needs, and give her the chance to live a safer and more dignified life.\r\n\r\nAnd if you are unable to donate, simply sharing our story means more than you could ever imagine.\r\n\r\nThank you for opening your heart to my little girl.\r\n\r\nMay God bless you and your family.\r\n\r\nWith all my love and gratitude,\r\n\r\nMaria, Vexanna's Mom","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-vexanna/1784260940-712b8a84.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-vexanna/1784260940-712b8a84.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/help-vexanna/1784260940-55b3bef1.jpeg"],"raised":87400,"goal":250000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Vexanna","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jane Cotta","amount":"$250","time":"9 minutes ago","message":"Praying for you, sweet Vexanna. No child should have to endure so much pain. I hope this donation helps bring you the care and comfort you deserve. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Julian Brown","amount":"$20","time":"21 minutes ago","message":"Your story broke my heart. I'm sending my donation today and praying that God surrounds your family with strength, hope, and healing. ❤️"},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Stay strong, little angel. Your beautiful smile is stronger than this disease. May God bless you and your amazing mom. 🙏💚"},{"name":"William Gomes","amount":"$100","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Every child deserves the chance to live without pain. I hope many people see your story and come together to help. Sending love from my family. ❤️"},{"name":"Pamela Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"2 hours ago","message":"I can't imagine what your mother has gone through. No parent should ever face something like this alone. Praying for miracles and brighter days ahead. 🙏"},{"name":"Uilson Ramirez","amount":"$30","time":"3 hours ago","message":"Just made a donation. It's not much, but I hope it helps. Wishing Vexanna a future filled with healing, peace, and happiness. ❤️"},{"name":"Vania Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"3 hours ago","message":"Your courage is truly inspiring. May God continue watching over you and bless everyone who helps your family through this difficult journey. 🙏💕"},{"name":"Uesley Miller","amount":"$50","time":"4 hours ago","message":"I have children, and your story brought tears to my eyes. I'm praying that compassionate people around the world come together to help Vexanna. ❤️"}],"donations_count":"2.9k","created_at":"2026-07-17T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-les","slug":"help-les","title":"Retire 83-Year-Old Les and Help Save His Home","description":"Hi, my name is Samuel Weidenhofer, and I am fundraising for Les.\n\nLes is 83 years old, a veteran, and still works four days a week at Lowe's. Heartbreakingly, he is considering going back full time because the bills are no longer covering the basic cost of life.\n\nHe is working to care for his sick wife and repay the medical bills that have continued piling up. He never imagined reaching 84 years old and needing to work full time just to save their home and make sure they still have somewhere to live.\n\nLes is one of a kind and one of the kindest people I have ever met. He helped me even while he was struggling himself. Now I hope our community can come together and give him the chance to retire.\n\nHe deserves to spend the time he has left beside his wife instead of worrying every day about another shift, another bill or whether they will lose their home.\n\nEvery contribution can help cover medical debt, household expenses and the urgent costs that are keeping Les at work. If you cannot donate, sharing his story or leaving kind words can still help us reach someone who can.\n\nLet's retire Les, because no 83-year-old veteran should be forced to work just to keep a roof over his family.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-les/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-les/1.webp"],"raised":83650,"goal":200000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Samuel Weidenhofer","location":"United States","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"947","created_at":"2026-07-28T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://us.brighthorizonfd.com/samuelb"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-olivia","slug":"olivia","title":"Help Olivia Live with Dignity","description":"My name is Olivia. I am 19 years old, and I live with muscular dystrophy.\n\nLittle by little, this disease has taken away my ability to move. Today, I cannot walk, get out of bed on my own, or do even the simplest daily tasks. My wheelchair and my bed are where I spend almost my entire life.\n\nBut there is one person who has never left my side.\n\nMy mom.\n\nShe has devoted her entire life to taking care of me. Every morning she lifts me out of bed and into my wheelchair. She helps me bathe, get dressed, eat, and takes care of all my daily needs. She is the one who takes me to every doctor’s appointment, every medical exam, and every treatment. She is with me every hour of every day.\n\nShe isn’t just my mother.\n\nShe is my caregiver, my strength, my best friend, and the reason I keep smiling through all of this.\n\nThe hardest part is knowing how much she has sacrificed for me.\n\nBecause I depend on her for absolutely everything, she cannot have a job. She has spent nearly two decades caring for me 24 hours a day. While others are able to build careers and plan their futures, my mom spends every day lifting me, helping me change positions, caring for our home, arranging my treatments, and making sure I have everything I need.\n\nShe has given me her entire life without ever asking for anything in return.\n\nBut love doesn’t pay the bills.\n\nToday we are struggling just to cover our basic household expenses. Watching my mom worry about how we will make it through another month breaks my heart, because I know she already carries more than anyone should.\n\nThe wheelchair I use today is the same one I have had for 18 years.\n\nIt has worn out over time and no longer provides the support and safety my body needs. As my muscular dystrophy progresses, sitting for long periods becomes more painful, and transferring me becomes harder for my mom. A new wheelchair would not only improve my comfort—it would make my daily life safer and reduce the physical strain on the woman who cares for me every single day.\n\nWe also desperately need an accessible van.\n\nFor many people, transportation is something they never think about. For us, every hospital visit, every medical appointment, and every treatment is a major challenge. My mom has to struggle every time she moves me because we don’t have a vehicle designed for someone in my condition.\n\nAn accessible van would change our lives. It would allow me to travel safely and make every trip much easier for my mom, who has carried this responsibility almost entirely on her own for 19 years.\n\nMuscular dystrophy is a progressive disease. My muscles continue to weaken, and my dependence grows with each passing year. I cannot change that reality, but I still hope for a life with a little more comfort, dignity, and less suffering for my mother.\n\nI am not asking for luxury.\n\nI am asking for the chance to make life a little easier for the woman who has sacrificed everything for me, and for the opportunity to continue receiving the medical care I need.\n\nIf you can donate or simply share my story, you will be helping not only me, but also the incredible mother who has never stopped fighting for her daughter.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read my story.\n\nMay God bless you and your family.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/olivia/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/olivia/1.png","uploads/campaigns/olivia/2.png"],"raised":80812,"goal":115000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Olivia Daves","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Emily Carter","amount":"$50","time":"12 minutes ago","message":"Your story touched my heart. I'm praying that you receive your new wheelchair and accessible van soon. God bless you and your wonderful mother. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Michael Anderson","amount":"$100","time":"27 minutes ago","message":"No mother should have to carry this burden alone. Wishing you both strength, hope, and brighter days ahead. ❤️"},{"name":"Jessica Wilson","amount":"$25","time":"49 minutes ago","message":"I hope this donation helps even a little. Your mother's love is beautiful, and you both deserve so much support. 🙏"},{"name":"Daniel Thompson","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Praying that God opens every door for your family. May your fundraiser reach its goal quickly. Stay strong! ❤️"},{"name":"Amanda Brooks","amount":"$35","time":"2 hours ago","message":"Your strength is inspiring, Olivia. I'm praying for comfort, peace, and many blessings for you and your amazing mom. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Christopher Hall","amount":"$500","time":"4 hours ago","message":"Every young person deserves dignity and proper care. I hope you get the wheelchair and van your family needs. God bless you both."},{"name":"Rachel Morgan","amount":"$75","time":"7 hours ago","message":"Sending love, prayers, and hope from my family to yours. May God continue giving your mother strength every single day. ❤️"},{"name":"David Miller","amount":"$150","time":"10 hours ago","message":"You are stronger than you know, Olivia. Keeping you and your mom in my prayers. Better days are coming. 🙏❤️"}],"donations_count":"1000","created_at":"2026-02-02T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/olivia/"},{"id":"sarah","slug":"sarah","title":"Help Save Sarah Jones: Her Only Chance Is a Second Stem Cell Transplant","description":"My name is Sarah Jones.\r\n\r\nNot long ago, I underwent a stem cell transplant, hoping it would finally give me a chance to beat cancer and rebuild my life. Sadly, my disease returned sooner than expected.\r\n\r\nBecause my relapse happened within the required waiting period, my healthcare funding will not cover a second stem cell transplant. Even though my doctors believe this second transplant is my only real chance for a cure, the procedure is not being funded due to the enormous financial risk and the potential cost of complications.\r\n\r\nHearing this news has been absolutely devastating. Knowing that there is a treatment that could save my life, yet being unable to receive it because of financial barriers, is something I never imagined I would face.\r\n\r\nThis second stem cell transplant is not just another treatment—it is my best and only hope of beating this disease. Every day that passes without treatment gives the cancer more time to progress and reduces my chances of recovery.\r\n\r\nMy family and I are doing everything we can to raise the funds needed to move forward with this life-saving transplant. Unfortunately, the cost is far beyond what we could ever afford on our own.\r\n\r\nI never thought I would have to ask for help again, but today I have no other choice. If you are able to donate, share my story, or keep me in your prayers, you will be giving me something priceless—another chance at life.\r\n\r\nThank you from the bottom of my heart for your kindness, generosity, and support. Every donation, every share, and every prayer brings me one step closer to the treatment that could save my life.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/sarah/1783493969-66942782.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/sarah/1783493969-66942782.png"],"raised":77580,"goal":100000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Sarah Jones","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jane Cotta","amount":"$250","time":"18 minutes ago","message":"Praying for you, Sarah. No one should ever have to fight for life and finances at the same time. Donated and shared. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Julian Brown","amount":"$100","time":"42 minutes ago","message":"Your strength is truly inspiring. I hope this donation helps you get the transplant you need. Everyone, please donate if you can."},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"1 hour ago","message":"I don't know you, but I care about what you're going through. I pray Jehovah gives you the strength each day, and that those helping you have the wisdom, the knowledge, and the empathy needed to truly support you through this. I wanted to help, even in a small way. I look forward to the day when this is no longer your reality when \"… no resident will say: 'I am sick.'\" (Isa 33:24)"},{"name":"William Gomes","amount":"$20","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Cancer has already taken so much from you. I'm praying this transplant gives you the second chance you deserve. God bless you. ❤️"},{"name":"Pamela Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"2 hours ago","message":"Just donated. I hope many others join in. Together we can help Sarah receive this life-saving treatment."},{"name":"Uilson Ramirez","amount":"$250","time":"2 hours ago","message":"You are not fighting alone, Sarah. Keeping you in my prayers every day. Stay strong. 🙏"},{"name":"Vania Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"3 hours ago","message":"This broke my heart. Everyone who reads this, please consider donating or sharing. Every contribution matters."},{"name":"Uesley Miller","amount":"$20","time":"5 hours ago","message":"I wish I could give more. Sending love, prayers, and hoping your fundraiser reaches its goal very soon. ❤️"}],"donations_count":"5,3k","created_at":"2026-06-15T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"a6166b98-e4a2-4fd2-95d5-9cba968e9694","slug":"help-ross","title":"Help Ross Access Critical Cancer Treatment","description":"To my lovely supporters, old and new, I wanted to update you on how my week has been.\n\nI was discharged from the Ron Johnson Ward on Monday after spending time there fighting two infections and taking a break from chemotherapy for one cycle. That gave me a genuinely lovely week at home, recovering and rebuilding not only my strength but also my confidence, which has been tested recently.\n\nMonday was my seventh wedding anniversary, so we went out for dinner to celebrate. During the week, I visited Richmond Park with Stanley, my dog, and spent some time in nature. It was calming and restorative in a way I truly needed.\n\nOn Saturday, I celebrated a friend's birthday and got dressed up for dinner at his house. On Sunday, I visited Bournemouth, my hometown, to see my mum, dad and extended family. It was the first time I had been back since my diagnosis.\n\nThere were many positive moments in one week, and they reminded me exactly what this fight is worth. Throughout all of it, I have been taking care of myself, saving the energy I have for the things that matter most and resting whenever needed.\n\nNow I have until Thursday to prepare for my next round of treatment — full power this time.\n\nThank you, as always, for standing with me through this. Your support is helping me continue fighting for access to the cancer treatment I urgently need.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-ross/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-ross/1.webp"],"raised":72970,"goal":280000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Ross","location":"United Kingdom","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"660","created_at":"2026-07-28T00:00:00+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://us.brighthorizonfd.com/rossb"},{"id":"ayuda-cristian","slug":"ayuda-cristian","title":"Ayuda a Cristian Sanchéz a Seguir Luchando por su Vida","description":"Mi nombre es Rosa y soy la abuela de Cristian Sanchéz. Hoy me veo obligada a pedir ayuda porque ya no tengo fuerzas para seguir enfrentando esta lucha sola.\r\n\r\nNunca imaginé que, a mi edad, tendría que pedir ayuda para mantener con vida a mi nieto. Pero la vida nos puso frente a una prueba que ninguna familia debería vivir.\r\n\r\nCristian fue diagnosticado con un tumor maligno en el recto, un tipo de cáncer muy agresivo que requiere tratamiento constante, medicamentos, estudios médicos y atención especializada. La enfermedad le provoca fuertes dolores, un gran desgaste físico, debilidad extrema y muchas dificultades para moverse. Hoy necesita usar pañales, depende de ayuda para realizar la mayoría de sus actividades diarias y también necesita una silla de ruedas para poder desplazarse con un poco más de dignidad y seguridad.\r\n\r\nPero el dolor de Cristian no es solo físico.\r\n\r\nHace algunos años perdimos a mi hija, su madre, en un trágico accidente de tránsito. Fue un golpe que destrozó a toda nuestra familia. Poco tiempo después, cuando el padre de Cristian supo que su hijo tenía cáncer, decidió abandonarlo. Nunca volvió. Nunca envió dinero, nunca preguntó cómo estaba, nunca le ofreció una sola palabra de apoyo.\r\n\r\nComo si todo eso no fuera suficiente, la novia de Cristian también lo dejó cuando más la necesitaba.\r\n\r\nImaginen el dolor de un joven que ha perdido a su madre, fue abandonado por su padre y por la persona que amaba, mientras lucha contra un cáncer que pone su vida en riesgo cada día. Poco a poco dejó de sonreír y hoy también enfrenta una profunda depresión causada por tanto sufrimiento, soledad y abandono.\r\n\r\nQuien cuida de Cristian soy yo.\r\n\r\nPero yo también soy una mujer mayor.\r\n\r\nMi esposo, el abuelo de Cristian, es diabético y también necesita cuidados diarios. Paso las 24 horas del día atendiendo a los dos, administrando medicamentos, ayudándolos en todo lo que necesitan y tratando de mantenerlos con esperanza. Debido a esta situación ya no puedo trabajar y nuestros ingresos no alcanzan para cubrir las necesidades más básicas del hogar.\r\n\r\nCada mes luchamos para conseguir dinero para los medicamentos, los pañales, los alimentos, los estudios médicos, el transporte hacia los hospitales y todo lo que Cristian necesita para continuar su tratamiento. Muchas veces tengo que elegir qué necesidad atender primero, y esa es una decisión que rompe mi corazón.\r\n\r\nEscribo estas palabras con lágrimas en los ojos porque mi mayor miedo es no poder darle a mi nieto la oportunidad de seguir luchando por su vida.\r\n\r\nSi usted puede ayudarnos con cualquier donación, por pequeña que sea, estará dando esperanza a un joven que ha sufrido más de lo que cualquier persona debería soportar. Y si no puede colaborar económicamente, le pido de todo corazón que comparta nuestra historia.\r\n\r\nQue Dios bendiga a cada persona que se tome unos minutos para leer este mensaje y extender su mano a nuestra familia.\r\n\r\nCon todo mi agradecimiento,\r\n\r\nRosa, abuela de Cristian Sanchéz","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ayuda-a-cristian-sanch-z-a-seguir-luchando-por-su-vida/1784694517-a03f51d4.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/ayuda-a-cristian-sanch-z-a-seguir-luchando-por-su-vida/1784694517-a03f51d4.png","uploads/campaigns/ayuda-a-cristian-sanch-z-a-seguir-luchando-por-su-vida/1784694517-077976e5.png","uploads/campaigns/ayuda-a-cristian-sanch-z-a-seguir-luchando-por-su-vida/1784694517-6273e756.png"],"raised":57690,"goal":87000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"organizer":"Cristian Sanchéz","words_of_support":[{"name":"Valentina Morales","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 16 minutos","message":"Ningún niño debería luchar contra el cáncer y el abandono al mismo tiempo. Estoy orando por ti, Cristian. No pierdas la esperanza. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"María González","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Tu historia me rompió el corazón. Espero que esta pequeña ayuda sirva para tu tratamiento y tus necesidades diarias. Que Dios bendiga a toda tu familia. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"José Martínez","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Te envío un fuerte abrazo y muchas oraciones. Deseo de todo corazón que muy pronto lleguen días mejores para ti. ❤️"},{"name":"Ana Rodríguez","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"No estás solo, Cristian. Hay muchas personas que creemos en tu recuperación y estamos contigo. Mucha fuerza. 🙏"},{"name":"Carlos Hernández","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 4 horas","message":"Rezo para que Dios te dé fuerzas para seguir luchando. Nunca pierdas la fe. ❤️"},{"name":"Miguel Torres","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 5 horas","message":"Tus abuelos son unos verdaderos héroes. Espero que esta ayuda les dé un poco de tranquilidad en estos momentos tan difíciles. 🙏"},{"name":"Sofía Ramírez","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 5 horas","message":"Nadie merece pasar por tanto sufrimiento. Que Dios te conceda salud, paz y esperanza. ❤️"},{"name":"Alejandro López","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 7 horas","message":"Tu historia me hizo llorar. Espero que esta donación ayude con tu silla de ruedas, tus pañales y tu tratamiento. Sigue luchando, campeón. 🙏❤️"}],"donations_count":"1,9k","created_at":"2026-05-11T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"help-save-marks","slug":"help-save-marks","title":"Please Donate to Stop Mark's Severe Pain and Help Save His Life","description":"Your small donation will help stop Mark’s pain.\nGod Bless You!\n\nEvery touch on Mark’s skin can cause a new wound. For most of us, a hug is a simple gesture of love. For Mark’s, it can mean unbearable pain.\n\nShe was born with a rare genetic condition called Epidermolysis Bullosa, a cruel disease that makes her skin so fragile that even the slightest friction can cause painful blisters, open wounds, and life-threatening infections.\n\nImagine living like this from the very first day of life.\n\nWhile other children are learning how to crawl, play, and explore the world, Mark’s is fighting something no child should ever have to face: constant pain.\n\nEvery single day, her family must spend hours carefully changing bandages and treating her wounds to prevent dangerous infections. Without this care, the consequences can be devastating.\n\nBut there is hope.\n\nWith proper treatment, specialized bandages, and ongoing medical care, it is possible to ease her suffering and give Mark’s something every child deserves: a chance to live with less pain and more dignity.\n\nThe problem is that these treatments are extremely expensive. And that’s why we are asking for your help.\n\nToday, you have the power to make a real difference.\n\nA donation — no matter the amount — can help provide the bandages, medication, and essential medical care that keep Mark’s safe. It may seem small, but for a child who fights through pain every single day, it can mean everything.\n\nPlease help us give Mark’s the chance to experience a childhood with more hope and less suffering.\n\n❤️ Donate now and become part of this story of compassion.\n\nBecause no child should have to grow up fighting just to survive.\n\nHow Your Donation Helps:\n\nPain Medicine: Daily medications to manage her severe pain and make each day bearable.\n\nSpecial Bandages: Life-saving wound care bandages that must be changed daily to prevent infection.\n\nNutritional Meals: Specialized nutrition to support wound healing and her fragile immune system.\n\nMedical Care: Doctor visits, treatments, and the specialized care she needs to survive.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-save-marks/1.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-save-marks/1.jpeg"],"raised":52888,"goal":80000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Mark","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"6,4k","created_at":"2025-12-02T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"goyito","slug":"goyito","title":"💪 Goyito — Crawls Every Day Just to Survive and Care for His Mother","description":"💪 Goyito — Crawls Every Day Just to Survive and Care for His Mother\r\nGoyito (Gregorio’s nickname) was born with a rare physical condition. He cannot support himself on his legs, and his arms are twisted and curved, making even the simplest movements extremely painful and difficult.\r\n\r\nYet every single day, Goyito wakes up and goes to work — not to beg, but to survive.\r\n\r\nBecause he cannot walk, Goyito must crawl on the ground to move from place to place. This is the only way he can work, collect recyclable materials, and earn a few dollars a day.\r\n\r\nHe doesn’t ask for pity. He works with what life gave him.\r\n\r\n💔 His Reality\r\nMonths ago, Goyito lost his father. Since then, he has carried an even heavier burden: taking care of his mother completely on his own.\r\n\r\nEvery dollar he earns goes toward food and, most importantly, medicines his mother needs to survive. The income is very small, but the effort is enormous.\r\n\r\nWhen asked why he works so hard, Goyito answers:\r\n“She gave her life for me when I was little. Now it’s my turn to give everything for her.”\r\n\r\n⚠️ A Daily Risk No Human Should Face\r\nCrawling on the ground every day exposes Goyito to constant danger:\r\n\r\nOpen wounds and infections\r\nSevere pain in arms, spine, and joints\r\nPermanent worsening of his condition\r\nLife-threatening health complications over time\r\nWithout help, Goyito’s body is slowly breaking down. With support, he can regain dignity, safety, and hope.\r\n\r\n🎯 Our Goal: $100,000\r\nThis fundraiser exists to give Goyito and his mother a real chance at life. The goal of $100,000 will be used in stages:\r\n\r\n✅ Stage 1 – $30,000: Immediate Survival & Medical Support\r\nMedicines and medical care for his mother\r\nFood, hygiene items, and basic living expenses\r\nMedical evaluations for Goyito’s condition\r\n✅ Stage 2 – $40,000: Mobility & Health Preservation\r\nAdaptive mobility equipment to stop crawling on the ground\r\nTherapy and medical support to prevent further damage\r\nOngoing treatments, follow-ups, and pain management\r\n✅ Stage 3 – $30,000: Stability, Safety & Dignity\r\nSafer living conditions and basic accessibility improvements\r\nSupport tools so Goyito can work with less risk\r\nEmergency reserve for future medical and survival needs\r\n🕯️ Why This Matters\r\nGoyito’s story is not about weakness — it’s about courage. Choosing honest work, even when life is unbearably unfair.\r\n\r\nYour help can turn survival into dignity.\r\n\r\nA Call for Help\r\n🤲 Please help Goyito continue fighting.\r\n\r\n💵 Any amount — $5, $10, or more — makes a real difference.\r\n\r\n📢 If you can’t donate, sharing his story already helps tremendously.\r\n\r\nMessage from Goyito\r\n“God keeps me alive and gives me strength. I only ask for the chance to keep taking care of my mother.”\r\n\r\nYour Impact\r\nYou can be the reason Goyito stops crawling.\r\nYou can be the reason he works with dignity.\r\nYou can be the reason his mother gets the medicines she needs.\r\n\r\n🕊️ Help Goyito rebuild his future. Donate now.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/goyito/1784760777-c02c53bd.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/goyito/1784760777-c02c53bd.jpg"],"raised":48750,"goal":100000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Gregorio's","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jane Cotta","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Stay strong, Goyito! 🙏"},{"name":"Julian Brown","amount":"$20","time":"2 hours ago","message":"Sending so much love to you and your family. It’s heartbreaking to see you go through this, but please know you have an entire community rooting for your recovery. Don’t lose hope."},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"5 hours ago","message":"God bless you, Goyito. Praying for a miracle. ✨"},{"name":"William Gomes","amount":"$100","time":"8 hours ago","message":"I’ve been following your story for a few days now and couldn’t sit idle. I know words are small compared to what you’re facing, but I hope this contribution helps ease the burden slightly. Keep fighting, Goyito. Your strength is inspiring."},{"name":"Pamela Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"11 hours ago","message":"Time is critical, so I acted fast. Hoping this helps speed up the process for you. Please keep us updated on your progress. We are all watching and hoping for the best."},{"name":"Uilson Ramirez","amount":"$30","time":"12 hours ago","message":"Stay positive. Healing vibes coming your way! 💪"},{"name":"Vania Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"16 hours ago","message":"It’s incredible to see how people come together in moments like this. I just made my donation and encouraged my friends to do the same. We are all behind you, Goyito. Keep your head up and focus on healing. We’ve got your back."},{"name":"Uesley Miller","amount":"$50","time":"20 hours ago","message":"Small contribution from my side. It’s not much, but it’s sent with all my heart. Hope it helps with the treatment costs. You are not alone in this."}],"donations_count":"1,6k","created_at":"2026-06-21T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"goyito-es","slug":"goyito-es","title":"💪 Goyito — Gatea todos los días solo para sobrevivir y cuidar de su madre","description":"💪 Goyito — Se arrastra a diario solo para sobrevivir y cuidar a su madre\n\n Goyito (el apodo de Gregorio) nació con una condición física poco común. No puede sostenerse sobre sus piernas y sus brazos están retorcidos y arqueados, lo que hace que incluso los movimientos más simples sean extremadamente dolorosos y difíciles.\n\nSin embargo, cada día Goyito se levanta y sale a trabajar; no para pedir limosna, sino para sobrevivir.\n\nComo no puede caminar, Goyito debe arrastrarse por el suelo para desplazarse de un lugar a otro. Es la única forma que tiene de trabajar, recolectar materiales reciclables y ganar unos pocos dólares al día.\n\nNo pide lástima. Trabaja con lo que la vida le dio.\n\n💔 Su realidad\n\n Hace meses, Goyito perdió a su padre. Desde entonces, carga con una responsabilidad aún mayor: cuidar a su madre completamente solo.\n\nCada dólar que gana se destina a la comida y, lo más importante, a las medicinas que su madre necesita para sobrevivir. Sus ingresos son muy escasos, pero su esfuerzo es enorme.\n\nCuando le preguntan por qué trabaja tan duro, Goyito responde:\n\n «Ella dio su vida por mí cuando yo era pequeño. Ahora me toca a mí darlo todo por ella».\n\n⚠️ Un riesgo diario al que ningún ser humano debería enfrentarse\n\n Arrastrarse por el suelo a diario expone a Goyito a peligros constantes:\n\nHeridas abiertas e infecciones\n\n Dolor intenso en brazos, columna y articulaciones\n\n El deterioro permanente de su condición\n\n Complicaciones de salud que ponen en riesgo su vida a largo plazo\n\n Sin ayuda, el cuerpo de Goyito se está deteriorando poco a poco. Con apoyo, puede recuperar su dignidad, seguridad y esperanza.\n\n🎯 Nuestra meta: 100.000 dólares\n\n Esta campaña de recaudación de fondos existe para brindarles a Goyito y a su madre una oportunidad real de vida. La meta de 100.000 $ se destinará a las siguientes etapas:\n\n✅ Etapa 1 – 30.000 $: Supervivencia inmediata y apoyo médico\n\n Medicamentos y atención médica para su madre\n\n Alimentos, artículos de higiene y gastos básicos de subsistencia\n\n Evaluaciones médicas para la condición de Goyito\n\n ✅ Etapa 2 – 40.000 $: Movilidad y preservación de la salud\n\n Equipo de movilidad adaptado para evitar que se arrastre por el suelo\n\n Terapia y apoyo médico para prevenir daños mayores\n\n Tratamientos continuos, seguimiento médico y control del dolor\n\n ✅ Etapa 3 – 30.000 $: Estabilidad, seguridad y dignidad\n\n Condiciones de vida más seguras y mejoras básicas de accesibilidad\n\n Herramientas de apoyo para que Goyito pueda trabajar con menos riesgos\n\n Reserva de emergencia para futuras necesidades médicas y de supervivencia\n\n 🕯️ Por qué es importante\n\n La historia de Goyito no trata sobre la debilidad, sino sobre el coraje. Se trata de elegir un trabajo honesto, incluso cuando la vida es insoportablemente injusta.\n\nTu ayuda puede transformar la supervivencia en dignidad.\n\nUn llamado a la ayuda\n\n 🤲 Por favor, ayuda a Goyito a seguir luchando.\n\n💵 Cualquier cantidad —5 $, 10 $ o más— marca una diferencia real.\n\n📢 Si no puedes donar, compartir su historia ya es de gran ayuda.\n\nMensaje de Goyito\n\n «Dios me mantiene con vida y me da fuerzas. Solo pido la oportunidad de seguir cuidando a mi madre».\n\nTu impacto\n\n Puedes ser la razón por la que Goyito deje de arrastrarse.\n\n Puedes ser la razón por la que trabaje con dignidad.\n\n Puedes ser la razón por la que su madre reciba los medicamentos que necesita.\n\n🕊️ Ayuda a Goyito a reconstruir su futuro. Dona ahora.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/goyito-es/1784761860-a4d5ed00.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/goyito-es/1784761860-a4d5ed00.jpg"],"raised":48750,"goal":100000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"organizer":"Gregorio","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jane Cotta","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 16 minutos","message":"Acabo de donar. ¡Mantente fuerte, Goyito! 🙏"},{"name":"Julian Brown","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Envío mucho amor a ti y a tu familia. Es desgarrador ver lo que estás pasando, pero por favor sabe que tienes toda una comunidad rezando por tu recuperación. No pierdas la esperanza."},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"¡Compartido con mi red de contactos! Ayudemos a correr la voz. 📢"},{"name":"Juan Pérez","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 4 horas","message":"He estado siguiendo tu historia estos días y no podía quedarme de brazos cruzados. Sé que las palabras son pequeñas comparadas con lo que enfrentas, pero espero que esta contribución ayude a aliviar un poco la carga. Sigue luchando, Goyito. Tu fuerza es inspiradora."},{"name":"María García","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 5 horas","message":"Dios te bendiga, Goyito. Rezo por un milagro. ✨"},{"name":"Carlos Rodríguez","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 8 horas","message":"Una pequeña contribución de mi parte. No es mucho, pero la envío con todo mi corazón. Espero que ayude con los gastos del tratamiento. No estás solo en esto."},{"name":"Ana Martínez","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 12 horas","message":"Es increíble ver cómo la gente se une en momentos como este. Acabo de hacer mi donación y animé a mis amigos a hacer lo mismo. Todos estamos contigo, Goyito. Mantén la cabeza alta y concéntrate en sanar. Te respaldamos."},{"name":"Miguel Ángel Silva","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 13 horas","message":"Mantén la positividad. ¡Te envío vibras de sana! 💪"}],"donations_count":"1,6k","created_at":null,"stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"ayuda-ricardo","slug":"ayuda-ricardo","title":"Mi esposo no quiere morir. Solo quiere vivir para ver crecer a nuestro hijo.","description":"Mi nombre es Ana Rodríguez, y hoy escribo estas palabras con el corazón completamente destrozado.\r\n\r\nMi esposo, Ricardo Rodríguez, fue diagnosticado con cáncer de colon, una enfermedad agresiva que se desarrolla en el intestino grueso y que, poco a poco, va consumiendo no solo el cuerpo, sino también la esperanza de toda una familia.\r\n\r\nNuestra vida cambió por completo.\r\n\r\nEl hombre fuerte, trabajador y lleno de sueños que siempre sostuvo nuestro hogar hoy está extremadamente debilitado. El cáncer y los tratamientos han dejado a Ricardo muy débil. Ha perdido mucho peso, vive con dolores constantes, casi no puede comer, pasa la mayor parte del tiempo acostado y cada día tiene menos fuerzas para levantarse de la cama. Además, los tratamientos le provocan náuseas, vómitos, pérdida del apetito, un cansancio extremo y una debilidad que le impide realizar incluso las actividades más simples.\r\n\r\nA pesar de todo el sufrimiento que enfrenta, hay una frase que repite todos los días mientras mira a nuestro pequeño hijo:\r\n\r\n“No quiero morir… solo quiero vivir para ver crecer a mi hijo.”\r\n\r\nNo existe un dolor más grande para una esposa que escuchar esas palabras y no saber cómo aliviar ese miedo.\r\n\r\nRicardo ya no puede trabajar debido a la enfermedad. Y yo tampoco puedo hacerlo, porque debo cuidarlo las 24 horas del día. Él depende de mí para tomar sus medicamentos, ayudarlo a levantarse, acompañarlo a sus consultas y estar a su lado en cada momento de esta difícil batalla.\r\n\r\nNuestra única prioridad ahora es luchar por su vida.\r\n\r\nSin ingresos, nuestra situación se ha vuelto desesperada. Además de los gastos de consultas, estudios, medicamentos, alimentación especial y transporte para sus tratamientos, hoy también nos cuesta comprar alimentos y cubrir las necesidades más básicas de nuestro pequeño hijo.\r\n\r\nNunca imaginé que tendría que pedir ayuda públicamente, pero hoy no nos queda otra opción.\r\n\r\nSi puedes hacer una donación, sin importar el monto, estarás ayudando a que Ricardo continúe con su tratamiento, pueda acceder a los medicamentos que necesita y que nuestro hijo tenga lo indispensable mientras seguimos luchando por mantener unida a nuestra familia.\r\n\r\nY si en este momento no puedes colaborar económicamente, te pido de todo corazón que compartas nuestra historia. Tal vez llegue a alguien que pueda darnos una oportunidad para seguir adelante.\r\n\r\nEn nombre de mi esposo Ricardo, de nuestro hijo y de toda nuestra familia, gracias por tomarte el tiempo de leer nuestra historia.\r\n\r\nQue Dios bendiga tu vida y la de tu familia.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ayuda-ricardo/1784696879-7b1bf771.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/ayuda-ricardo/1784696879-7b1bf771.png"],"raised":47850,"goal":87000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"organizer":"Ricardo Rodríguez","words_of_support":[{"name":"Ashley Moore","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 37 minutos","message":"Estoy orando por Ricardo y por toda su familia. Que Dios les dé fuerzas para seguir luchando. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Christopher Taylor","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 51 minutos","message":"Ningún padre debería vivir con el miedo de no ver crecer a su hijo. Espero que esta ayuda les sirva. Dios los bendiga."},{"name":"Amanda Anderson","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Su historia me conmovió profundamente. Mucha fuerza para Ricardo, Ana y su pequeño hijo."},{"name":"Matthew Thomas","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Estoy rezando por un milagro. Ricardo, sigue luchando. Tu hijo te necesita. ❤️"},{"name":"Pamela Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"No pude contener las lágrimas al leer su historia. Espero que pronto lleguen más personas a ayudar."},{"name":"Uilson Ramirez","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 3 horas","message":"Que Dios bendiga a toda su familia. Nunca pierdan la esperanza. Estamos con ustedes."},{"name":"Vania Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 5 horas","message":"Una pequeña ayuda con mucho cariño. Espero que Ricardo pueda continuar su tratamiento."},{"name":"Christopher Taylor","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 5 horas","message":"Estoy compartiendo esta campaña para que llegue a más personas. Mucha fuerza."}],"donations_count":"1,5k","created_at":"2026-05-15T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-armando","slug":"armando","title":"Soy Lucía Fernández. Nunca imaginé que algún día tendría que pedir ayuda para salvar al hombre que amo.","description":"Mi nombre es Lucía Fernández y hoy escribo con el corazón completamente destrozado.\n\nMi esposo, Armando, siempre fue el sostén de nuestro hogar. Era él quien salía todos los días a trabajar, quien luchaba para que nunca faltara comida en nuestra mesa y quien hacía todo lo posible por cuidar de nuestra familia. Siempre fue un hombre fuerte, trabajador y lleno de esperanza.\n\nPero la enfermedad cambió nuestras vidas por completo.\n\nSu hígado está gravemente dañado y ya no funciona como debería. Todos los días veo al hombre que amo sufrir dolores intensos en todo su cuerpo. Su abdomen permanece muy inflamado debido a la enfermedad, vive con un cansancio extremo y muchas veces ni siquiera puede levantarse de la cama.\n\nComo si eso no fuera suficiente, Armando también padece un grave problema en la garganta que le impide comer con normalidad. Cada bocado se ha convertido en un momento de dolor. Ver a la persona que amas sufrir incluso para tragar un poco de comida es algo que rompe el corazón.\n\nAdemás, también sufre una inflamación en el colon que le provoca aún más dolor y limita completamente su calidad de vida.\n\nHoy mi esposo ya no puede caminar por sí solo. Necesita una silla de ruedas para poder asistir a sus consultas médicas, realizar estudios e incluso desplazarse dentro de nuestra propia casa. Poco a poco fue perdiendo su independencia y ahora depende de mí para casi todo.\n\nYo también tuve que dejar mi trabajo para cuidarlo las 24 horas del día. No puedo dejarlo solo ni un instante. Esto significa que nuestra familia se quedó sin ningún ingreso justo cuando los gastos comenzaron a ser más altos que nunca.\n\nLos medicamentos que necesita son muy costosos. Además, Armando utiliza tres paquetes de pañales cada semana y necesita una crema especial para proteger su piel, junto con consultas médicas, estudios, una alimentación adecuada y todos los cuidados que requiere su enfermedad. Cada semana aparece un nuevo gasto y, lamentablemente, ya no tenemos cómo afrontarlo.\n\nNunca pensé que tendría que pedir ayuda a personas que no conozco. Siempre trabajamos con esfuerzo y dignidad para salir adelante. Pero hoy no estamos pidiendo lujos; solo estamos pidiendo una oportunidad para que Armando pueda continuar su tratamiento y vivir con un poco menos de dolor.\n\nCualquier donación, por pequeña que sea, nos ayudará a comprar sus medicamentos, los pañales, la crema especial, la silla de ruedas que tanto necesita y a cubrir los gastos básicos de nuestro hogar mientras seguimos luchando contra esta enfermedad.\n\nY si en este momento no puedes donar, te pido de todo corazón que compartas nuestra historia. Tal vez llegue a la persona indicada y pueda cambiar el destino de nuestra familia.\n\nEn nombre de Armando y de toda nuestra familia, gracias por tomarte el tiempo de leer nuestra historia. Que Dios bendiga profundamente a cada persona que decida extendernos su mano en este momento tan difícil.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/armando/1.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/armando/1.jpeg"],"raised":40627,"goal":50000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Armando Fernández","location":"Ubicación no especificada","words_of_support":[{"name":"María González","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 8 minutos","message":"Lucía, no pude contener las lágrimas al leer la historia de Armando. Rezo para que Dios les dé fuerzas y que muy pronto pueda recibir la silla de ruedas y todos los medicamentos que necesita. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Carlos Ramírez","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 14 minutos","message":"Nadie debería pasar por tanto sufrimiento. Espero que esta pequeña ayuda alivie un poco la carga de su familia. Mucha fuerza, Armando. Dios está con ustedes. 🙏"},{"name":"Sofía Herrera","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 22 minutos","message":"Qué difícil debe ser cuidar a la persona que amas viendo cómo sufre todos los días. Lucía, eres una mujer muy valiente. Que Dios los bendiga siempre. ❤️"},{"name":"Miguel Torres","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 35 minutos","message":"Espero de todo corazón que puedan comprar la silla de ruedas y continuar con el tratamiento. Mucha fuerza para toda la familia. No pierdan la esperanza. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Andrea Castillo","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 41 minutos","message":"Aunque mi ayuda sea pequeña, la envío con mucho cariño. Estaré orando por la recuperación de Armando y por la fortaleza de Lucía. ❤️"},{"name":"José Martínez","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Ninguna familia debería tener que elegir entre comprar medicamentos o llevar comida a casa. Espero que muchas personas se unan para ayudar a Armando. Dios los bendiga. 🙏"},{"name":"Valentina Rojas","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Compartí su historia con toda mi familia. Confío en que llegarán muchas personas de buen corazón para apoyar esta causa. Mucha fuerza. ❤️"},{"name":"Fernando López","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Que Dios haga un milagro en la vida de Armando. Espero que muy pronto pueda aliviar su dolor y recuperar un poco de calidad de vida. Un fuerte abrazo para ustedes. 🙏❤️"}],"donations_count":"434","created_at":"2026-06-11T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/armando/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-thiago","slug":"thiago","title":"Ayuda a Salvar la Vida de Mi Hijo Thiago","description":"Mi nombre es Lourdes Jesús, y escribir estas palabras es una de las cosas más difíciles que he tenido que hacer en toda mi vida.\n\nNunca imaginé que tendría que pedir ayuda a personas que no conozco para intentar salvar a mi hijo.\n\nThiago tiene apenas 7 años. Debería estar corriendo, jugando, yendo a la escuela y disfrutando de la infancia que todo niño merece. Pero, en lugar de eso, pasa sus días entre hospitales, análisis, agujas y sesiones de quimioterapia, luchando contra una enfermedad devastadora llamada Leucemia Linfoblástica Aguda (LLA).\n\nLa leucemia es un cáncer que afecta la médula ósea e impide que el cuerpo produzca células sanguíneas sanas. Como consecuencia, su organismo pierde la capacidad de combatir infecciones, transportar oxígeno y controlar las hemorragias. Un simple resfriado puede poner en riesgo su vida.\n\nCada día veo a mi pequeño sufrir.\n\nLa quimioterapia es extremadamente agresiva. Le provoca fuertes dolores, un cansancio insoportable, náuseas constantes, vómitos, fiebre, pérdida de cabello y una debilidad tan intensa que muchas veces ni siquiera puede levantarse de la cama. Hay días en los que no puede comer, jugar o incluso sonreír.\n\nNo existe un dolor más grande para una madre que escuchar a su hijo pedir que el dolor termine y no poder hacer nada para aliviarlo.\n\nDesde que recibimos el diagnóstico, tuve que dejar de trabajar para cuidarlo las 24 horas del día. Thiago depende completamente de mí. Lo acompaño en cada consulta, cada hospitalización y cada tratamiento. No puedo dejarlo solo ni un instante.\n\nEso significa que hoy no tenemos ninguna fuente de ingresos.\n\nMientras luchamos por salvar la vida de mi hijo, también enfrentamos otra batalla: poder cubrir las necesidades más básicas de nuestro hogar. Necesitamos ayuda para comprar alimentos, medicamentos, pagar el transporte al hospital, el alquiler, los servicios y todo lo necesario para seguir adelante.\n\nLos gastos médicos son enormes y continúan aumentando. Muchas veces me pregunto cómo voy a conseguir el dinero para el siguiente tratamiento o simplemente para poner un plato de comida sobre la mesa.\n\nA pesar de todo el dolor que enfrenta, Thiago sigue siendo un niño lleno de sueños. Me pregunta cuándo podrá volver a correr, jugar con otros niños y vivir una infancia normal.\n\nYo sigo creyendo que ese día llegará.\n\nPero no puedo librar esta batalla sola.\n\nHoy, con toda la humildad de mi corazón, les pido que nos ayuden. Cualquier donación, por pequeña que sea, nos acerca un poco más a la esperanza. Su apoyo nos permitirá continuar con el tratamiento de Thiago, comprar sus medicamentos, cubrir los traslados al hospital y sostener las necesidades básicas de nuestra familia mientras seguimos luchando por su vida.\n\nY si en este momento no pueden donar, por favor compartan nuestra historia. Un simple gesto puede llegar a la persona indicada y convertirse en el milagro que tanto necesitamos.\n\nDe madre a madre, de padre a padre, de corazón a corazón…\n\nPor favor, ayúdennos a darle a mi hijo la oportunidad de seguir viviendo.\n\nQue Dios bendiga a cada persona que decida tendernos una mano.\n\nCon todo mi amor y eterna gratitud,\n\nLourdes Jesús\n\nMamá de Thiago. ❤️","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/thiago/1.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/thiago/1.jpg","uploads/campaigns/thiago/2.jpg"],"raised":40627,"goal":50000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Thiago Jesús","location":"Ubicación no especificada","words_of_support":[{"name":"María Fernández","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 8 minutos","message":"Lloré al leer la historia de Thiago. Ningún niño debería pasar por tanto dolor. Espero que mi pequeña ayuda les dé un poco de alivio. Dios los bendiga. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Carlos Ramírez","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 21 minutos","message":"Estoy orando por Thiago todos los días. Que Dios guíe a los médicos y le conceda una pronta recuperación. Mucha fuerza para ti, Lourdes. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Sofía Herrera","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 34 minutos","message":"No puedo imaginar el sufrimiento que están viviendo. Envío este aporte con todo mi cariño y mis oraciones. ❤️"},{"name":"Javier Morales","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Los niños merecen una oportunidad para vivir y ser felices. Espero que esta donación ayude a Thiago a seguir luchando. Que Dios haga un milagro. 🙏"},{"name":"Fernando Rojas","amount":"$75","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Me rompió el corazón conocer todo lo que ha pasado Thiago. Oro para que muy pronto pueda volver a jugar como cualquier niño. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Camila Mendoza","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Dios está con ustedes incluso en los momentos más difíciles. Que nunca pierdan la esperanza. Un fuerte abrazo para Thiago y su mamá. ❤️"},{"name":"Daniela Ortiz","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 3 horas","message":"Mi hijo tiene casi la misma edad que Thiago y no pude contener las lágrimas. Estoy rezando por su sanación completa. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Andrés López","amount":"$150","time":"Hace 6 horas","message":"Los niños como Thiago nos enseñan lo valientes que pueden ser incluso en medio del sufrimiento. Estoy con ustedes en oración. 💙🙏"}],"donations_count":"434","created_at":"2026-06-11T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/thiago/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-save-castiel","slug":"save-castiel","title":"Help save Castiel’s life fighting Stage 4 Cancer","description":"Castiel is joy personified. He’s bright-eyed, full of giggles, cuddly beyond measure—the kind of baby who reaches out for you and instantly steals your heart. He is the light of his parents’ lives. He is also adored deeply by his big brother, Nicollas—a sweet, gentle 13-year-old on the autism spectrum. Just recently, Mike and Leidiane noticed a bump on Castiel’s head. Then another on his neck. Concerned, they brought him in for an ultrasound. They waited two agonizing days for that appointment. Within an hour of leaving that office came the call that turned their world upside down: “Take him to Children’s Hospital—immediately.” Castiel has been diagnosed with Stage Four High-Risk Neuroblastoma. Dozens of tumors have been found throughout his tiny body—his spine, kidneys, lungs, skull, neck, and bones. He is only a baby, but he is already in the fight of his life. Since his diagnosis, Castiel has endured more than any child should: • His first full five-day round of chemotherapy• A bone marrow extraction• Two blood transfusions• Multiple biopsies He’s only at the beginning of what will be an aggressive and invasive treatment plan: more transfusions, scans, surgeries, radiation, and ongoing chemo lie ahead. His body is already reacting—he’s in pain, with sores in his mouth, fighting through side effects he can’t possibly understand. He’s also teething right now—a cruel reminder of the milestones he should be reaching, of the baby life he should be living. Mike and Leidiane are also doing everything they can to support Nicollas, who thrives with consistency, routine, and close attention. Ensuring he feels safe and cared for during this time is just as essential—and presents an added layer of emotional and logistical challenge as they navigate hospital visits, appointments, and long days away from home. Nicollas and Castiel’s parents are kind, humble, and giving to the core. If you know them, you know this. If you don’t, just know that the love they pour into others is now being poured into their boys—with every ounce of strength they have. We’re raising funds to help cover:\n\n️Extensive medical expenses not covered by insurance\n\n️ Travel, parking, and lodging for hospital visits\n\n️ Meals and daily expenses during extended stays\n\n️Lost income, as both parents must miss work\n\n️ Childcare and support for Nicollas No family is prepared for this. But we believe in the strength of community to carry a family through what no one should face alone. If you can give—please, do. Every dollar counts. If you can’t, please share. And above all, hold this family in your heart and prayers. Castiel is a warrior in footie pajamas. He’s fighting. So we will, too—beside him, for him, and with unshakable hope. Thank you for standing with Castiel.With love and gratitude.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/save-castiel/90815937_1780760592172402_r-1-768x1024.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/save-castiel/90815937_1780760592172402_r-1-768x1024.jpg","uploads/campaigns/save-castiel/90815937_1747269898523875_r-768x960.png","uploads/campaigns/save-castiel/90815937_177093552744463_r-1-768x960.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/save-castiel/90815937_1754843428119803_r-768x1024.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/save-castiel/90815937_1747269936832538_r-768x960.png"],"raised":40400,"goal":100000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Castiel Davis","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"John Davis","amount":"$20","time":"35 minutes","message":"I hope this campaign reaches everyone who can help you continue your treatment. Stay strong, little warrior!"},{"name":"Emily Carter","amount":"$35","time":"3 hours","message":"No child should have to fight alone. I hope more people join this campaign and help Castiel and other families facing the same difficult journey."},{"name":"Michael Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"1 day","message":"Sending love, strength, and prayers to Castiel and her family. Every contribution matters, so please help if you are able."},{"name":"Sarah Thompson","amount":"$15","time":"3 days","message":"I cannot give much, but I believe many small acts of kindness can create something powerful. Keep fighting, Castiel!"},{"name":"Daniel Martinez","amount":"$100","time":"5 days","message":"This campaign is not only about one child. It is about giving hope to families who cannot afford the treatment their children desperately need."},{"name":"Olivia Wilson","amount":"$25","time":"14 days","message":"Castiel deserves the chance to grow, play, and experience a beautiful childhood. Please donate and share this campaign with others."},{"name":"Victor Davis","amount":"$20","time":"2 months","message":"God bless you little one"},{"name":"Udson Miller","amount":"$50","time":"4 months","message":"Jesus loves you❤️"}],"donations_count":"1928","created_at":"2026-02-05T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/save-castiel/"},{"id":"shamila","slug":"shamila","title":"Please Donate to Stop Shamila's Severe Pain and Help Save Her Life","description":"Your small donation will help stop Shamila’s pain.\nGod Bless You!\n\nRight now…a little girl named Shamila is suffering in a way most people can’t even imagine.\n\nShe was born with a rare and devastating condition called Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB).\n\nThis disease makes her skin so fragile that it cannot hold itself together.\n\nAny touch…any movement…even her own body…\n\ncan tear her skin apart.\n\nFor you, a hug means love.For Shamila… it can mean intense, unbearable pain.\n\nChildren like her are often called “butterfly children”…because their skin is as delicate as butterfly wings.\n\nBut the truth is much more brutal.\n\nShe lives in pain — every single day.\n\nBlisters form constantly.Wounds open again and again.And the pain feels like severe burns that never stop.\n\nImagine living like this from the very first day of life.\n\nWhile other children are learning to laugh, play, and explore…Shamila is fighting something no child should ever face:\n\nconstant suffering.\n\nEvery day, her family spends hours caring for her wounds:\n\ncarefully removing bandages stuck to her skin\n\ncleaning open sores\n\ntrying to prevent infections that could take her life\n\nEvery moment… is a battle.\n\nAnd there is something even harder to accept:\n\nThere is no cure.\n\nThe only way to keep Shamila alive is through:\n\npain medication\n\nspecialized bandages\n\nconstant medical care\n\nWithout this… her pain becomes unbearable.And the risks become life-threatening.\n\nBut there is hope — and it starts with you.\n\nWith the right treatment, it’s possible to ease her pain…to protect her fragile body…and to give her something every child deserves:\n\na chance to live with less suffering.\n\nThe problem is…\n\nThese treatments are expensive.And her family cannot do this alone.\n\nToday, you have the power to change her reality.\n\nA small donation can help provide:\n\npain relief so she doesn’t suffer every second\n\nlife-saving bandages to protect her wounds\n\nproper nutrition to support healing\n\nessential medical care to keep her alive\n\nIt may seem small to you…\n\nBut for Shamila…it means everything.\n\nWhile some people will scroll past this…others will choose to act.\n\nThe difference is simple:\n\nsome watch… others save lives.\n\nChoose your amount below:\n\n15$ – Buys 6 Full Days of Pain Medicine30$ – Buys 12 Full Days of Pain Medicine50$ – Buys 19 Full Days of Pain Medicine100$ – Buys 20 Full Days of Life-Saving Special Bandages250$ – Buys 30 Days of Pain Medicine, 30 Days of Life-Saving Special Bandages plus 30 Days of Wound-Healing Nutritional Meals","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/shamila/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/shamila/1.webp","uploads/campaigns/shamila/2.webp","uploads/campaigns/shamila/3.webp","uploads/campaigns/shamila/4.webp","uploads/campaigns/shamila/5.webp","uploads/campaigns/shamila/6.webp","uploads/campaigns/shamila/7.webp"],"raised":32347,"goal":50000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Shamila","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"3,3k","created_at":"2026-01-20T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"help-save-gwen","slug":"help-save-gwen","title":"Please Donate to Stop Lily's Severe Pain and Help Save Her Life","description":"Today… I am fighting for my life.\n\nNot long ago, I heard something no one is ever prepared to hear:“You have 6 to 9 months to live.”\n\nThe cancer has already spread… and since that moment, nothing has been the same.\n\nMy life now revolves around chemotherapy, hospitals, tests… and pain, every single day.There are days I wake up with no strength. Days where all I can do is try to endure just a little longer.\n\nWhile the world keeps moving outside… I am here, fighting to stay alive.\n\nAnd it’s not just my body that’s affected.My entire life has changed.\n\nMy income has dropped, but the bills haven’t stopped.Medical costs keep rising.And even in the middle of all this… I still have to find the strength to recover.\n\nCancer doesn’t wait… and neither do the challenges that come with it.\n\nThat’s why I’m asking for help.\n\nI never wanted to be in this position, but right now, I truly need it.Any contribution, no matter how small, makes a real difference in my life.\n\nIt helps me continue my treatment,cover basic living expenses,and keep going without giving up.\n\nI don’t know what tomorrow will look like…but today, I’m still here.\n\nStill fighting.Still trying.Still holding on to hope.\n\nIf you can help me, I will be deeply grateful.\n\nYou can be part of my fight.And today… that means everything to me. 💚","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-save-gwen/1.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-save-gwen/1.jpeg"],"raised":26400,"goal":35000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Gwen Rodriguez","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"942","created_at":"2026-03-05T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-kaleb","slug":"kaleb","title":"Help Kaleb Keep Fighting","description":"Kaleb is a little boy whose life has been a battle since the day he was born.\n\nHe was diagnosed with a rare intestinal disease that prevents his body from absorbing the nutrients he needs to survive. While most children grow stronger with every meal, Kaleb’s body cannot. Without specialized medical care, his life is constantly at risk.\n\nTo stay alive, Kaleb depends on parenteral nutrition, receiving the nutrients his body cannot absorb directly into his bloodstream through a central catheter. This treatment is not optional—it is what keeps him alive.\n\nEvery single day is filled with challenges.\n\nHis family carefully monitors everything. Chronic diarrhea and severe dehydration can quickly become life-threatening. Even something as simple as drinking too much water must be controlled with precision. A small mistake can lead to serious complications, emergency hospital visits, or dangerous infections.\n\nBut the hardest part is that the treatment doesn’t end when Kaleb leaves the hospital.\n\nAt home, his family follows a demanding routine that no child should ever have to endure. Every day includes catheter care, strict hygiene, medical appointments, therapies, medications, and constant monitoring to protect him from infections and keep him stable.\n\nThe financial burden has become overwhelming.\n\nThe costs never stop. Medical supplies, diapers, medications, therapies, laboratory tests, transportation to hospitals and specialists, and the equipment needed for his daily care continue to grow month after month.\n\nDespite everything he faces, Kaleb continues to smile.\n\nHe dreams, laughs, and finds joy in the little moments, showing a strength far beyond his years. His family does everything possible to give him the chance to grow, play, and experience the childhood every child deserves.\n\nToday, we are asking for your help.\n\nYour donation will go directly toward Kaleb’s ongoing medical care, therapies, medications, essential supplies, transportation, and the everyday expenses required to keep him healthy and safe.\n\nNo contribution is too small. Every act of kindness helps relieve the burden on his family and gives Kaleb another chance to keep fighting.\n\nThank you for standing with Kaleb and reminding his family that they are not facing this journey alone.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/kaleb/ka-rq80s77sxur9gibxju9ofduha19xc1slax59cx5mjc.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/kaleb/ka-rq80s77sxur9gibxju9ofduha19xc1slax59cx5mjc.jpg","uploads/campaigns/kaleb/kaleb-catheter-care-rq80s85n4osjs4akecoazvlxvf5ajqwbn1squ748d4.jpg","uploads/campaigns/kaleb/kaleb-daily-insumos-rq80s93hbitu3q978v2xkddegt0nrg01z6g8bh2u6w.jpg","uploads/campaigns/kaleb/kaleb-smile-rq80sa1bicv4fc7u3dhk4v4v26w0z53sbb3psr1g0o.jpg"],"raised":26400,"goal":35000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Kaleb Jones","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Emily Carter","amount":"$50","time":"12 minutes ago","message":"Praying for you, Kaleb. May God continue to protect you and give your family strength every single day. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Michael Thompson","amount":"$100","time":"27 minutes ago","message":"No child should have to fight a battle like this. I just donated and will keep your family in my prayers. Stay strong, little warrior. 💙"},{"name":"Sarah Mitchell","amount":"$30","time":"46 minutes ago","message":"Sending love, prayers, and hope. Every donation makes a difference. God bless you, Kaleb. 🙏"},{"name":"David Wilson","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Just made my donation. Wishing Kaleb continued strength and better days ahead. ❤️"},{"name":"Jessica Brown","amount":"$20","time":"2 hours ago","message":"I wish I could give more. Keeping Kaleb and his family in my prayers. May God watch over all of you. 🙏💙"},{"name":"Ryan Anderson","amount":"$150","time":"3 hours ago","message":"Let's show this family they are not alone. Every share and every donation helps bring hope. 💙"},{"name":"Ashley Davis","amount":"$80","time":"5 hours ago","message":"Your story touched my heart. Praying for healing, comfort, and brighter days ahead for sweet Kaleb. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Christopher Moore","amount":"$500","time":"7 hours ago","message":"May God continue to bless and strengthen your family. Kaleb, you are an incredible little fighter. Keep believing. 💙🙏"}],"donations_count":"942","created_at":"2026-03-05T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/kaleb/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-alliyah","slug":"alliyah","title":"Help Give Alliyah a Chance to Heal","description":"My name is Sarah Jhonson, and writing these words is one of the hardest things I have ever had to do.\n\nSince the day my daughter, Alliyah, was born, my life has been devoted entirely to caring for her. She lives with a severe condition that has caused a massive growth on her head. Watching my little girl grow up facing so many challenges breaks my heart every single day.\n\nWhile other children are running, playing, and discovering the world, Alliyah faces struggles that no child should ever have to endure. Every day is filled with constant care, medical appointments, uncertainty, and hope that one day she will receive the treatment that could change her life.\n\nAs a mother, there is no greater pain than watching your child suffer while knowing you cannot provide everything she needs. I do everything I can to care for her with all the love in my heart. I feed her, comfort her through the difficult moments, and try to hide my tears so she never loses hope. But when the day comes to an end, I often find myself wondering how we will make it through another tomorrow.\n\nThe cost of medical consultations, diagnostic tests, medications, transportation, daily necessities, and ongoing treatment is far beyond what our family can afford. Every new medical appointment brings another financial burden that feels impossible to overcome.\n\nMore than anything, I want my daughter to have the opportunity to receive the medical care she deserves. I dream of seeing her live with less pain, more comfort, and the hope of a brighter future.\n\nToday, I am putting my pride aside and opening my heart. I never imagined I would have to ask for help, but a mother will do absolutely anything to save her child.\n\nIf you are able to donate, please know that every contribution will go directly toward Alliyah’s medical treatment, examinations, medications, transportation, and the daily expenses our family faces throughout this journey.\n\nIf you are unable to donate, simply sharing our story could help it reach someone who can.\n\nFrom the bottom of my heart, thank you for taking the time to read our story. Your kindness gives us the strength to keep believing that better days are still ahead.\n\nMay God bless you and your family.\n\nWith love and gratitude,\n\nSarah Jhonson\n\nAlliyah’s Mother","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/alliyah/Meet-rqdk4oa2oi7cfw6k6v8ftyrtp7gdnui792dinnrkr0.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/alliyah/Meet-rqdk4oa2oi7cfw6k6v8ftyrtp7gdnui792dinnrkr0.png"],"raised":25548,"goal":45000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Alliyah Jhonson","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Michael Carter","amount":"$100","time":"12 minutes ago","message":"No child should have to endure so much pain. We are praying for you every day, Alliyah. May God bless you and your family. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Jessica Williams","amount":"$50","time":"28 minutes ago","message":"Your story touched my heart. Stay strong, sweet girl. I hope this small gift brings you one step closer to the treatment you deserve."},{"name":"David Thompson","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Praying for a miracle for Alliyah. May God guide every doctor caring for her and give strength to her wonderful mother."},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$75","time":"2 hours ago","message":"No family should have to face this alone. Sending love, prayers, and support from my family to yours. ❤️"},{"name":"Christopher Miller","amount":"$150","time":"3 hours ago","message":"Keep believing. There is still hope, and there are people around the world praying for Alliyah's recovery. God bless your family."},{"name":"Daniel Wilson","amount":"$500","time":"8 hours ago","message":"May this donation help give Alliyah the opportunity she deserves. Never lose faith. God is with your family every step of the way."},{"name":"Ashley Brown","amount":"$30","time":"5 hours ago","message":"I wish I could do more. I will continue praying for you and sharing your story. Stay strong, beautiful girl. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Olivia Martinez","amount":"$40","time":"10 hours ago","message":"Sending love from our family. We are praying that Alliyah receives the treatment she needs and has a brighter future ahead. ❤️🙏"}],"donations_count":"636","created_at":"2026-03-03T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/alliyah/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-emma-eb","slug":"help-emma-eb","title":"Help Emma Access Specialized Epidermolysis Bullosa Care","description":"Emma is three years old and lives with Epidermolysis Bullosa, a rare condition that makes her skin extremely fragile. Ordinary movement, clothing and daily routines can cause skin injuries that require careful treatment.\n\nHer father, Mark, works in construction while the family manages Emma's ongoing care. She needs specialized non-stick dressings, ointments, medication, protective clothing and regular medical supervision.\n\nThe campaign goal is $100,000 to help cover daily wound care supplies, essential medicines, specialist treatment, transportation and living costs connected to her care.\n\nEvery contribution can help Emma's family maintain the supplies and medical support she needs. If you can, support Emma's care today.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-emma-eb/emma-capa.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-emma-eb/emma-capa.png"],"raised":24992.1,"goal":100000,"currency":"USD","category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"829","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-isa","slug":"help-isa","title":"Help Isa Continue Her Cancer Treatment","description":"Isa, whose full name is Isabela, is four years old and is receiving care for an aggressive tumor in her stomach. Her treatment requires specialist consultations, chemotherapy, medication and continued hospital support.\n\nHer family is raising funds so her medical care can continue without interruption. Contributions can help cover treatment, medicines, transportation and the practical costs of staying close to her during care.\n\nThe campaign goal is $100,000. Every contribution can help Isa's family maintain access to the next stages of her treatment. If you can, support Isa's care today.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-isa/isa-capa.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-isa/isa-capa.jpeg"],"raised":24992.1,"goal":100000,"currency":"USD","category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"829","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-laura-cancer","slug":"help-laura-cancer","title":"Help Laura Access Specialized Skin and Wound Care","description":"Laura needs ongoing specialized skin and wound care. Her daily routine depends on careful dressing changes and reliable access to supplies her family cannot cover alone.\n\nShe needs non-stick bandages, medical ointments, supplements, protective clothing and continued medical supervision. These supplies are used quickly and must be replaced regularly.\n\nThe campaign goal is $100,000 to help with specialized supplies, medical supervision, transportation and related family expenses. Every contribution can support Laura's continuing care. If you can, support Laura today.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-laura-cancer/laura.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-laura-cancer/laura.webp"],"raised":24992.1,"goal":100000,"currency":"USD","category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"829","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-lucas-leukemia","slug":"help-lucas-leukemia","title":"Help Lucas Continue His Leukemia Treatment","description":"Lucas is a six-year-old boy receiving treatment for leukemia. His care includes chemotherapy, specialized medicines, medical supervision and hospital visits.\n\nHis family is raising funds to help maintain access to treatment and cover the related costs they cannot manage alone. Support can help with medicines, hospital care, transportation, accommodation and basic needs while a parent stays close to him.\n\nThe campaign goal is $100,000. Every contribution can help Lucas continue the care recommended for him. If you can, support Lucas's treatment today.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-lucas-leukemia/lucas.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-lucas-leukemia/lucas.webp"],"raised":24992.1,"goal":100000,"currency":"USD","category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"829","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-olivia","slug":"help-olivia","title":"Help Cure Olivia of Cancer","description":"Olivia is only three years old, and she is facing the biggest battle of her life.\n\nJust a short time ago, her world looked like any other little girl's. She loved chasing bubbles across the yard, laughing at cartoons, cuddling with her favorite stuffed animal and filling her home with smiles.\n\nShe should be spending her days discovering the world. Instead, she is spending them in hospital rooms.\n\nEverything changed when Olivia started feeling unwell. Her family hoped it was something simple, but a few appointments became countless hospital visits, blood tests, scans and days filled with fear. Then came the diagnosis no parent is prepared to hear: cancer.\n\nSince that day, Olivia has endured hospital stays, painful procedures, medication and treatments that no three-year-old should have to experience. Some days she does not have the energy to play. On the hardest days, her parents can only hold her hand and promise they will keep fighting together.\n\nHer family has rearranged their lives, exhausted their savings and devoted every moment to helping Olivia receive the care she needs.\n\nThe $100,000 goal will help cover life-saving chemotherapy and treatment, essential medicine, specialized hospital care, transportation, accommodation and basic living costs so her parents can remain beside her.\n\nEvery donation brings Olivia closer to healing and gives her family hope. If you cannot donate, sharing her story can help it reach someone who can.\n\nPlease help give Olivia the chance to grow up, return home and enjoy the childhood she deserves. ❤️","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-olivia/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-olivia/1.png"],"raised":24992.1,"goal":100000,"category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Olivia's Family","location":"","words_of_support":[{"name":"Claire Donovan","amount":"$149","time":"Recent support","message":"It breaks my heart to see Olivia suffering, and I hope this helps bring her some relief."},{"name":"Camila Duarte","amount":"$50","time":"Recent support","message":"I wish I could have given more, but I know it will still make a difference for Olivia's treatment."},{"name":"Alina Petrova","amount":"","time":"Recent support","message":"Wishing Olivia a future full of health, happiness, and strength. 💖"}],"donations_count":"829","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://donors-club.com/help-olivia/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-hilary","slug":"help-hilary","title":"Help Hilary Fight a Rare Cancer Relapse","description":"Hilary is only eight years old. After more than a year of treatment for an extremely rare cancer, she had to undergo the amputation of her right arm and part of her shoulder to stop the disease from advancing and protect her life.\n\nAbout Her Name\n\nIn Brazilian public reporting, she is known as Áurea. For international outreach, this campaign uses the name Hilary to help protect her privacy. Both names refer to the same brave child and the same medical journey.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-01.jpg|Hilary has kept smiling through hospital stays, procedures and treatment. Photo: Family archive, as published by G1 Santos.\n\nHow Her Fight Began\n\nHer family's fight began in April 2025, when they noticed a lump near her right elbow. An MRI revealed a tumor. After further examinations and biopsies at GRAACC, a children's cancer hospital in São Paulo, doctors identified PEComa — a rare tumor that develops from cells associated with blood vessels.\n\nHilary endured six cycles of chemotherapy and three surgeries. For a brief moment, her family believed the cancer was gone. They celebrated the news and tried to give her the childhood moments treatment had taken away.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-02.jpg|Even during treatment, Hilary continued finding moments to play, smile and enjoy being a child. Photo: Family archive, as published by G1 Santos.\n\nWhen the Cancer Returned\n\nOnly a few months later, the cancer returned in a more aggressive form. The tumor appeared near her armpit and again close to the elbow. Doctors tried two cycles of intensive ICE chemotherapy and later returned to the original treatment protocol, but the disease continued to progress.\n\nHer medical team explained that removing her right arm and part of her shoulder offered the best chance to save her life. The surgery took place on July 20. According to her family, the first pathology report found no disease in nine removed lymph nodes, but she still needs close monitoring and further examinations.\n\nWhen her family explained what the surgery meant, Hilary responded with extraordinary courage: she understood that it was being done so she could stay alive and get well.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-03.jpg|Hilary's journey before and after surgery shows the courage she carries into every stage of treatment. Photo: Family archive, as published by G1 Santos.\n\nHer New Dream: Independence\n\nHilary continues taking chemotherapy tablets at home every day. She returns to GRAACC every seven to fifteen days for medical follow-up, blood tests and care for her PICC line. Through all of this, her family says she keeps smiling, playing and going to school whenever she can.\n\nNow her greatest dream is a prosthetic arm. She wants more independence for the simple things children do every day — playing, getting dressed, studying and moving through life with greater freedom. The cost of the prosthesis is beyond what her family can manage alone.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-04.jpg|Behind every hospital visit is an eight-year-old girl who loves color, play and moments of normal childhood. Photo: Family archive, as published by G1 Santos.\n\nHow Your Support Helps\n\nThe campaign's $40,000 goal will help the family pursue a suitable prosthesis while meeting the ongoing costs of treatment, medical follow-up, medication, transportation and daily care. The campaign has raised $24,000, leaving $16,000 to reach that goal.\n\nEvery contribution can bring Hilary closer to greater independence and give her family breathing room while they remain focused on her recovery. If you cannot donate, sharing her story can help it reach someone who can.\n\nThank you for standing beside Hilary and her family.\n\nStory information reported by G1 Santos on August 11, 2026. Photos: Family archive, as published by G1 Santos.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/hilary-photo-clean-frame-2-2s.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/hilary-photo-clean-frame-2-2s.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-01.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-02.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-03.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-hilary/story-g1-04.jpg"],"raised":24000,"goal":40000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"","hide_social_proof":true,"words_of_support":[],"created_at":"2026-09-08T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://brightlifefoundation.com/help-hilary/","news_source_url":"https://g1.globo.com/sp/santos-regiao/noticia/2026/08/11/menina-de-8-anos-tem-braco-amputado-apos-volta-de-cancer-raro-e-sonha-com-protese-mais-autonomia.ghtml","source_attribution":"Story information reported by G1 Santos. Photos: Family archive, as published by G1 Santos."},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-help-miguel","slug":"help-miguel","title":"Don’t let Davi lose his brother Miguel.","description":"Miguel is just a little boy, but cancer has already caused severe swelling and pain in his legs, making every movement a struggle.\n\nEven through the pain, he continues to smile, play, and show incredible strength. But behind that smile is a family desperately searching for treatment options—and parents terrified of losing their child.\n\nMiguel also has a twin brother, Davi. They have been inseparable since birth. They play together, grow together, and share a bond that words cannot explain.\n\nDavi is too young to understand why his brother is suffering. He only knows that Miguel is always supposed to be by his side.\n\nThis family should not have to face this battle alone. Your donation can help Miguel access the medical care he urgently needs and give these two brothers the chance to continue growing up together.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-miguel/1a1d4131-4210-407c-94c7-4e0d12afc0e2.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-miguel/1a1d4131-4210-407c-94c7-4e0d12afc0e2.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-miguel/Captura-de-tela-2026-07-21-223439.png","uploads/campaigns/help-miguel/Captura-de-tela-2026-07-21-223305.png"],"raised":21548,"goal":39000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Miguel Williams","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Joe Frings","amount":"$500","time":"1 hour","message":"Sending love and encouragement. Good luck guys"},{"name":"Jonas Smith","amount":"$100","time":"6 hours","message":"I made a prayer for Miguel. May God save"},{"name":"Emily Garcia","amount":"$100","time":"21 hours","message":"I set my part, it's painful to see this brothers growing together."},{"name":"Will Miller","amount":"$250","time":"1 day","message":"Money raised from Leni’s raffle run by the amazing We Brought Beer in Tooting Market!"},{"name":"Piter Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"6 days","message":"If we all help a little, we can save her from this."},{"name":"United Lodge of Prudednce No.83","amount":"$50","time":"8 days","message":"On behalf of our Worshipful Master, Steve Pallett, and all the Brethren of the Lodge, we wish you well"},{"name":"Vander Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"1 month","message":"God bless you little one"},{"name":"Udson Estrella","amount":"$50","time":"2 months","message":"Sending love from Logan (Kido) and family."}],"donations_count":"1632","created_at":"2026-04-04T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/help-miguel/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-help-save-laura","slug":"help-save-laura","title":"Aid Laura: 40 Years of Service, Now in Need","description":"At 60 years old, Laura has spent countless hours serving others with kindness and warmth, making her a beloved figure to many who know her. She currently works as a server at our restaurant and she’s been doing it for almost 40 years! Yes, she is an incredible server and loves her job. She is the type of person who always lends a helping hand to others in need, and now she finds herself needing our support. I have been working with Laura for about 3 years and she’s one of the most selfless, caring, and determined people I have ever met. The Battle Ahead:Laura has been diagnosed with stage two invasive ductal breast cancer, which has spread to her lymph nodes. She will need to undergo surgery in the coming weeks, which will require her to take approximately 1.5 to 2 months off work. During this time, she will face significant challenges—not only the physical and emotional toll of her diagnosis but also financial strains that could affect her home. Financial Struggles:As a waitress, Laura relies on her income to manage her bills. Unfortunately, the loss of her paycheck during recovery will compound her financial difficulties. In addition, she is struggling to keep up with property taxes and is worried about losing her home. Her 16-year-old car is also in dire need of repairs, making it difficult for her to get to medical appointments or access essential resources. What Your Support Will Do:Your contributions will go toward:– Covering medical expenses related to her surgery and recovery.– Helping Laura pay her property taxes so she doesn’t lose her home.– Assisting with necessary car repairs to ensure she can access healthcare and support. How You Can Help:We understand that not everyone can contribute financially, but there are many ways to offer support:1. Share this Save a Life Foundation page with your network to help spread the word.2. Send your positive thoughts and prayers to Laura as she undergoes treatment.3. If you can, offer assistance with meals, transportation, or anything Laura might need during this difficult time. Conclusion:Laura Beth is a tenacious spirit who has always been there for others. Now, it’s our turn to be there for her as she fights this battle. Your generosity can make a significant difference in her life, providing much-needed relief during a challenging period. Laura has always been an incredible human to everyone she’s met and taken care of, and I can’t think of anyone else who deserves this help more than her. Thank you for considering supporting Laura. Together, we can help her through this difficult journey. Thank you and God bless.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-save-laura/Captura-de-Tela-2026-05-16-as-15.29.15-rnjzjhbj6wt61yjsxysp85ig9efbe3z0tg9x3zjlxo.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-save-laura/Captura-de-Tela-2026-05-16-as-15.29.15-rnjzjhbj6wt61yjsxysp85ig9efbe3z0tg9x3zjlxo.png","uploads/campaigns/help-save-laura/Captura-de-Tela-2026-05-16-as-15.28.43-rnjzjboi1wlg4arzuwcxt6xop3743xcmsod08bryz0.png","uploads/campaigns/help-save-laura/Captura-de-Tela-2026-05-16-as-15.28.21-rnjzj6zb3qf0i8ytmcbsyq4dq5ua1ftz413ktxyxu4.png","uploads/campaigns/help-save-laura/Captura-de-Tela-2026-05-16-as-15.26.58-rnjzivp8tpzkmxf7g7ga4syuljdvh2l72h9r2mfnws.png"],"raised":20812,"goal":35000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Laura Beth","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jimmy Martinez","amount":"$100","time":"1 hour","message":"Sending love and encouragement. Good luck guys"},{"name":"Jordan Anderson","amount":"$250","time":"10 hours","message":"All the best to you. We are all with you"},{"name":"Sarah Davis","amount":"$250","time":"1 day","message":"I will keep you in my prayers, that if you have faith in Jesus that even if you aren’t healed in this life know that if you ask Jesus into your heart and believe, what awaits you in eternity will be far greater than any pain we experience here on earth. I pray for your healing in the mighty name of Jesus Christ amen."},{"name":"We Brought Beer Tooting","amount":"$100","time":"3 days","message":"Through the difficulty of this storm the lord is with you. Lean on him in prayer and his word for strength. He will never forsake you or abandon you. There is no darkness his light can’t overcome and he will always be with your family. I hope and pray for beautiful moments to fill your lives together. Jesus loves you"},{"name":"Philip Ayers","amount":"$50","time":"6 days","message":"If we all help a little, we can save her from this pain."},{"name":"Uilson Rodriguez","amount":"$446","time":"8 days","message":"We hope that this helps your family and that you are able to get medical assistance that you need during this difficult time. We are sending you and your family positive vibes, and prayers your way!"},{"name":"Vania Smith","amount":"$5","time":"1m month","message":"God bless you little Laura"},{"name":"Udson Brown","amount":"$50","time":"2 months","message":"Sending love and prayers to your family. You are not alone."}],"donations_count":"1000","created_at":"2025-12-02T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/help-save-laura/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-save-erica","slug":"save-erica","title":"Help Erica Against Cancer and Brain Disease","description":"Help Erica Continue Her Medical Journey\n\nHi, my name is Erica. I am currently receiving care for medullary thyroid cancer, systemic T-cell lymphoma, and Idiopathic Intracranial Hypertension, also known as IIH.\n\nIIH is a rare neurological condition that causes increased pressure around the brain and requires ongoing medical attention. Over the past few years, my medical journey has included multiple procedures, a VP shunt, a venous sinus stent, kidney surgeries, and recovery from a stroke caused by elevated intracranial pressure.\n\nMy ongoing care includes prescribed medication, specialist appointments, medical testing, follow-up visits, and close monitoring of my overall health.\n\nThis personal medical fundraiser was created to help support the continuity of my treatment and care. Contributions will help with treatment-related needs, prescribed medication, specialist care, testing, follow-up appointments, and transportation connected to my medical journey.\n\nEvery contribution helps me continue focusing on my health and the care recommended by my medical team.\n\nIf you are not able to contribute, sharing this page can also make a meaningful difference by helping my story reach more people.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read my story and for supporting me throughout this journey.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/save-erica/99318049_1769448552969103_r-scaled.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/save-erica/99318049_1769448552969103_r-scaled.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/save-erica/99318049_1769448725936252_r-scaled.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/save-erica/WhatsApp-Image-2026-07-21-at-21.19.48-1.jpeg"],"raised":19812,"goal":40000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Erica Hills","location":"Not specified","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jimmy Martinez","amount":"$100","time":"1 hour","message":"Sending love and encouragement. Good luck Erica, we are Together"},{"name":"Jordan Anderson","amount":"$250","time":"10 hours","message":"All the best to you. We are all with you"},{"name":"Sarah Davis","amount":"$250","time":"1 day","message":"I will keep you in my prayers, that if you have faith in Jesus that even if you aren’t healed in this life know that if you ask Jesus into your heart and believe, what awaits you in eternity will be far greater than any pain we experience here on earth. I pray for your healing in the mighty name of Jesus Christ amen."},{"name":"We Brought Beer Tooting","amount":"$100","time":"3 days","message":"Through the difficulty of this storm the lord is with you. Lean on him in prayer and his word for strength. He will never forsake you or abandon you. There is no darkness his light can’t overcome and he will always be with your family. I hope and pray for beautiful moments to fill your lives together. Jesus loves you"},{"name":"Philip Ayers","amount":"$50","time":"6 days","message":"If we all help a little, we can save her from this pain."},{"name":"Uilson Rodriguez","amount":"$446","time":"8 days","message":"We hope that this helps your family and that you are able to get medical assistance that you need during this difficult time. We are sending you and your family positive vibes, and prayers your way!"},{"name":"Vania Smith","amount":"$5","time":"1m month","message":"God bless you little Erica"},{"name":"Udson Brown","amount":"$50","time":"2 months","message":"Sending love and prayers to your family. You are not alone Erica."}],"donations_count":"803","created_at":"2026-02-06T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/save-erica/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-jesus-lopez","slug":"jesus-lopez","title":"Mi hijo perdió un ojo y parte de su cerebro… y tengo miedo de que también pierda las ganas de vivir.","description":"Mi nombre es María López y soy la madre de Jesús López, un joven de apenas 15 años. Nunca imaginé que tendría que escribir estas palabras para pedir ayuda.\n\nHasta hace poco, mi hijo era un adolescente lleno de sueños. Le gustaba estudiar, jugar, salir con sus amigos y hablar sobre todo lo que quería hacer cuando fuera mayor. Nuestra vida era sencilla, pero éramos felices.\n\nTodo cambió en cuestión de segundos.\n\nUn terrible accidente estuvo a punto de quitarme a mi hijo para siempre. Durante horas, los médicos lucharon por salvar su vida. Gracias a Dios sobrevivió, pero las consecuencias fueron devastadoras.\n\nJesús perdió uno de sus ojos y también sufrió una lesión cerebral gravísima que le hizo perder parte de su cerebro. Desde ese día, nuestra vida nunca volvió a ser la misma.\n\nHoy mi hijo enfrenta desafíos que ningún niño debería vivir.\n\nLas secuelas neurológicas han provocado que poco a poco pierda movilidad. Hay días en los que le cuesta caminar, sostener objetos e incluso realizar tareas sencillas. Los médicos nos explicaron que necesita medicamentos de forma permanente, fisioterapia intensiva, consultas especializadas y rehabilitación constante para evitar que siga perdiendo funciones y movilidad.\n\nComo si todo esto no fuera suficiente, el único ojo que le queda también está perdiendo visión debido a las consecuencias del accidente. Necesita con urgencia unos lentes especiales para intentar preservar la poca visión que aún conserva.\n\nPero lo que más rompe mi corazón no son solamente las secuelas físicas.\n\nEs ver el enorme sufrimiento emocional que vive mi hijo.\n\nJesús necesita una prótesis ocular, cuyo costo es de 8.500 dólares. Esa prótesis no le devolverá la vista, pero sí puede devolverle algo que perdió el día del accidente: su autoestima.\n\nDesde que regresó a la escuela, su vida se convirtió en una pesadilla.\n\nHa sido víctima de burlas, insultos y acoso escolar. Algunos compañeros se ríen de su rostro, hacen comentarios crueles y lo señalan como si fuera diferente. El niño alegre que siempre sonreía ahora evita mirar a las personas.\n\nYa no quiere salir de casa.\n\nYa no quiere reunirse con sus amigos.\n\nCasi no sonríe.\n\nMuchas veces lo encuentro llorando solo en su habitación, preguntándome por qué tuvo que pasarle esto a él. Como madre, no existe un dolor más grande que ver cómo tu hijo pierde la ilusión de vivir mientras tú no puedes hacer nada para aliviar su sufrimiento.\n\nLos médicos también están preocupados por su estado emocional. El aislamiento, la vergüenza y el rechazo que vive todos los días están haciendo que entre en un cuadro de depresión.\n\nMientras tanto, los gastos no dejan de aumentar.\n\nAdemás de la prótesis ocular, debemos comprar los lentes especiales para proteger la visión que aún conserva, pagar medicamentos permanentes, fisioterapia, consultas médicas, exámenes, transporte para acudir a los tratamientos y cubrir las necesidades básicas de nuestro hogar. Desde el accidente he tenido que dedicar mi vida por completo al cuidado de Jesús y ya no puedo trabajar como antes.\n\nPor todo esto, nuestra meta es recaudar 25.000 dólares, una cantidad que nos permitirá cubrir la prótesis ocular, los lentes especiales, los medicamentos, la rehabilitación, las terapias y los gastos básicos que necesitamos para seguir luchando por la recuperación de mi hijo.\n\nJamás imaginé que tendría que pedir ayuda a personas que no conozco.\n\nPero hoy dejo de lado todo orgullo porque la salud, la dignidad y el futuro de mi hijo valen mucho más que cualquier vergüenza.\n\nSi puedes hacer una donación, no solo estarás ayudando a pagar un tratamiento.\n\nEstarás devolviéndole esperanza a un joven de apenas 15 años, que sueña con volver a sentirse aceptado, conservar la visión que le queda, recuperar parte de su movilidad y volver a sonreír sin miedo.\n\nSi en este momento no puedes ayudar económicamente, te pido de todo corazón que compartas nuestra historia. Un simple gesto puede llegar a la persona indicada y cambiar por completo el futuro de mi hijo.\n\nQue Dios bendiga tu vida y la de tu familia por tomarte unos minutos para conocer la historia de Jesús López.\n\nCon todo mi cariño y mi eterna gratitud,\n\nMaría López\n\nMadre de Jesús López","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/jesus-lopez/IMG_5251.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/jesus-lopez/IMG_5251.jpg","uploads/campaigns/jesus-lopez/IMG_5252.jpg"],"raised":15627,"goal":25000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Jesús López","location":"Ubicación no especificada","words_of_support":[{"name":"María González","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 8 minutos","message":"Rezo por ti, Jesús. Espero que muy pronto puedas recibir la prótesis y seguir luchando. Dios los bendiga. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Carlos Ramírez","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 12 minutos","message":"Nadie merece pasar por algo así. Mucha fuerza para Jesús y para toda su familia. ❤️"},{"name":"Lucía Fernández","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 19 minutos","message":"Lloré al leer esta historia. Espero que esta pequeña ayuda les acerque un poco más a la recuperación de Jesús. 🙏"},{"name":"Javier Morales","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 27 minutos","message":"Mucha fuerza, campeón. No permitas que las burlas apaguen tu esperanza. Dios está contigo. ❤️"},{"name":"Ana Rodríguez","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 34 minutos","message":"Como madre, esta historia rompió mi corazón. Que Dios bendiga a Jesús y le conceda una pronta recuperación. 🙏"},{"name":"Miguel Herrera","amount":"$40","time":"Hace 41 minutos","message":"Espero que miles de personas se unan para ayudar a este joven. Mucha fe y mucha fuerza. ❤️"},{"name":"Patricia Gómez","amount":"$75","time":"Hace 55 minutos","message":"Jesús merece una segunda oportunidad. Oro para que conserve la visión que le queda y pueda volver a sonreír. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Fernando Castillo","amount":"$150","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Que Dios les dé fuerzas para seguir adelante. Compartí su historia con mi familia. ❤️"}],"donations_count":"302","created_at":"2026-05-03T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/jesus-lopez/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-ricardo","slug":"ricardo","title":"Ayuda a Mi Hijo Ricardo Amparo a Seguir Luchando por su Vida","description":"Mi nombre es Francisca Amparo y jamás imaginé que algún día tendría que acudir a personas que no conozco para pedir ayuda. Pero cuando se trata de la vida de un hijo, una madre hace todo lo que está en sus manos.\n\nMi hijo Ricardo Amparo tiene apenas 7 años y está luchando contra el cáncer. Desde el día de su diagnóstico, nuestras vidas cambiaron por completo. La sonrisa de un niño lleno de sueños fue reemplazada por días de sufrimiento, hospitalizaciones, exámenes, agujas y sesiones de quimioterapia.\n\nVer a mi hijo pasar por todo esto rompe mi corazón. La quimioterapia le provoca un enorme desgaste físico: sufre fuertes dolores, náuseas constantes, pierde el apetito y queda tan débil que, algunos días, ni siquiera puede levantarse de la cama. Cada tratamiento representa una nueva batalla, y como madre, es devastador no poder aliviar todo el dolor que está soportando.\n\nLamentablemente, además de enfrentar esta terrible enfermedad, también estamos viviendo una difícil situación económica. Tuve que dejar de trabajar para dedicarme a cuidarlo las 24 horas del día, porque Ricardo depende completamente de mí. Al no poder trabajar, nuestros ingresos desaparecieron justo cuando los gastos médicos comenzaron a aumentar.\n\nHoy necesitamos ayuda para cubrir el costo de los medicamentos, los exámenes, las consultas médicas, el transporte hacia el hospital y los tratamientos que pueden darle una oportunidad de seguir viviendo. También estamos luchando para poder cubrir las necesidades más básicas de nuestro hogar, como la alimentación, los servicios y todo lo necesario para que Ricardo pueda enfrentar esta enfermedad con un poco más de dignidad.\n\nComo madre, mi mayor miedo es mirar a mi hijo y sentir que no puedo darle todo lo que necesita para continuar luchando por su vida. Mi único deseo es volver a verlo sano, corriendo, jugando y disfrutando de la infancia que el cáncer le arrebató demasiado pronto.\n\nSi puedes hacer una donación, sin importar el monto, estarás llevando esperanza a mi hijo. Y si en este momento no puedes ayudar económicamente, compartir nuestra historia también será un gesto inmenso de amor y solidaridad.\n\nDe madre a madre, de corazón a corazón, les suplico que nos ayuden. Seguimos creyendo en los milagros, y quizás tú puedas formar parte del milagro que salve la vida de mi pequeño.\n\nCon todo mi corazón,\n\nFrancisca Amparo\n\nMadre de Ricardo Amparo","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ricardo/IMG_5254.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/ricardo/IMG_5254.jpg","uploads/campaigns/ricardo/IMG_5253.jpg","uploads/campaigns/ricardo/IMG_5257.jpg"],"raised":15627,"goal":20000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Ricardo Amparo","location":"Ubicación no especificada","words_of_support":[{"name":"María González","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 4 minutos","message":"Soy madre y no puedo imaginar el dolor que estás viviendo. Oro por Ricardo todos los días. Mucha fuerza para tu familia. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Carlos Ramírez","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 9 minutos","message":"Espero que esta pequeña ayuda sirva para que Ricardo continúe su tratamiento. Que Dios los bendiga y les dé mucha fortaleza."},{"name":"Lucía Fernández","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 14 minutos","message":"Nadie debería ver sufrir a un niño de esta manera. Estoy orando por un milagro para Ricardo. ❤️"},{"name":"José Herrera","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 22 minutos","message":"Mucha fuerza, pequeño campeón. Sigue luchando. Estoy seguro de que saldrás adelante. Dios está contigo."},{"name":"Ana Martínez","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 31 minutos","message":"Tu historia me hizo llorar. Espero de todo corazón que muchas personas puedan ayudar a Ricardo. 🙏"},{"name":"Miguel Torres","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 40 minutos","message":"Ningún niño debería pasar por tanto dolor. Que este aporte ayude a aliviar un poco esta difícil batalla. Dios los bendiga."},{"name":"Sofía Navarro","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 52 minutos","message":"Estoy compartiendo esta campaña con todos mis amigos. Ricardo merece una oportunidad para vencer el cáncer. ❤️"},{"name":"Valentina Rojas","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Acabo de hacer mi donación. Que Dios bendiga a Ricardo y les dé la fuerza necesaria para superar esta prueba. 🙏❤️"}],"donations_count":"252","created_at":"2026-05-03T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/ricardo/"},{"id":"savesmyfather","slug":"savesmyfather","title":"Please Help My Dad Fight for His Life","description":"My name is Sarah, and I am creating this fundraiser because I have reached the most difficult moment of my life. I never imagined that one day I would have to ask strangers for help, but I no longer have anyone else to turn to.\r\n\r\nJust over a month ago, my father was diagnosed with severe coronary artery disease. The doctors discovered that several of the arteries supplying his heart were critically blocked, putting his life at constant risk. From that moment on, everything happened so quickly.\r\n\r\nShortly after his diagnosis, my father suffered two heart attacks in a row. While we were still trying to cope with everything and hoping he was finally beginning to recover, another emergency happened. I found him unconscious at home and had to call 911 immediately. He was rushed to the hospital, where he continues to receive medical care. Since then, his condition has remained extremely fragile, and we still face so much uncertainty about his recovery.\r\n\r\nMy father has been unable to work for over a month. The income we depended on disappeared just as our medical expenses began to grow. Doctor's appointments, tests, medications, and ongoing treatment have consumed the little money we had managed to save.\r\n\r\nWe recently moved to this city. We have no family nearby, we hardly know anyone, and we don't have a support system. It's just my father and me.\r\n\r\nOur biggest concern is no longer just his health. We are struggling to cover even our most basic living expenses. The rent is overdue, the food in our home is running out, and if things continue like this, I don't know how much longer we'll be able to stay in our home.\r\n\r\nCreating this fundraiser has been one of the hardest decisions of my life. We have always been hardworking people, and we never imagined we would find ourselves asking for help. But the truth is that I can no longer carry this burden alone.\r\n\r\nYour donation will help us cover my father's medical expenses, purchase the medications he urgently needs, keep a roof over our heads, and put food on our table while he continues fighting for his life and, we hope, recovers enough to work again someday.\r\n\r\nIf you are able to contribute, no matter the amount, please know that your generosity will make an incredible difference in our lives. And if you are unable to donate, simply sharing this fundraiser would mean more to us than words can express.\r\n\r\nThank you for taking the time to read our story and for any kindness or support you can offer during this incredibly difficult time. May God bless you and your family.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/savesmyfather/1782381543-047c7fd2.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/savesmyfather/1782381543-047c7fd2.png","uploads/campaigns/savesmyfather/1782381543-e238887b.jpeg","uploads/campaigns/savesmyfather/1782381543-c40e6835.png"],"raised":13450,"goal":20000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Sarah","words_of_support":[{"name":"Emily R.","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour ago","message":"My heart breaks for what Sarah and her father are going through. If you're able to help, even a small donation can make a real difference. Let's show them they're not alone. ❤️"},{"name":"Michael T.","amount":"$20","time":"2 hours ago","message":"No family should have to choose between medical care and putting food on the table. If this story touched your heart, please consider supporting them or sharing this fundraiser."},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"3 hours ago","message":"I can't imagine how difficult this must be. Every contribution, no matter how small, helps bring them one step closer to getting through this. Let's come together and help."},{"name":"William Gomes","amount":"$100","time":"6 hours ago","message":"Life can change in an instant. Today it's their family, tomorrow it could be ours. If you have the ability to help, please consider donating or sharing this campaign."},{"name":"Pamela Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"8 hours ago","message":"Sarah showed incredible courage by asking for help during such a difficult time. Let's remind her that kindness still exists. Every donation and every share truly matters."}],"donations_count":"458","created_at":"2026-06-25T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"saves-susan","slug":"saves-susan","title":"Please Help My Little Girl Smile Again","description":"My name is Susan, and I am Anthee's mother.\r\n\r\nI never imagined I would have to ask strangers for help to save my little girl, but today I have no other choice.\r\n\r\nAnthee is only 10 years old.\r\n\r\nShe should be worrying about school, making friends, playing outside, and dreaming about what she wants to be when she grows up. Instead, every single day, she wakes up wondering if people will laugh at her again.\r\n\r\nMy daughter was born with a rare genetic condition called Crouzon Syndrome, which caused the bones in her skull to fuse much too early. As her brain continued to grow, the pressure forced her eyes outward, changing her appearance and creating serious medical complications.\r\n\r\nWatching your child suffer physically is heartbreaking.\r\n\r\nWatching her lose her happiness is even worse.\r\n\r\nEvery day at school, Anthee is bullied because she looks different. Children point at her, whisper, laugh, and call her cruel names. Some refuse to sit next to her. Others stare at her as though she isn't a little girl with feelings.\r\n\r\nWhen we go outside, strangers often stop and stare. Some even reach out and touch her face out of curiosity, without asking, without realizing how deeply it hurts her.\r\n\r\nI watch my daughter pretend she's okay...\r\n\r\nBut when we get home, she cries.\r\n\r\nShe asks me why she can't look like everyone else.\r\n\r\nShe asks me why people are so mean.\r\n\r\nAs a mother, there are no words painful enough to describe those moments.\r\n\r\nOver time, the constant bullying has stolen the light from her beautiful smile. The little girl who used to laugh all day has become quiet, withdrawn, and afraid of the world around her.\r\n\r\nToday, Anthee is also battling depression. She often begs me not to send her to school because she's terrified of being laughed at again. No ten-year-old child should have to carry that kind of pain.\r\n\r\nHer struggles don't end there.\r\n\r\nBecause of Crouzon Syndrome, she has difficulty breathing, suffers from frequent infections, and cannot fully close her eyes while she sleeps.\r\n\r\nEvery single night, before I put my daughter to bed, I gently tape her eyelids shut to protect her eyes from drying out and being permanently damaged.\r\n\r\nEvery night, I kiss her forehead and silently pray that one day she won't have to live like this anymore.\r\n\r\nDespite everything, Anthee is still the sweetest little girl. She still dreams of having friends. She still dreams of going to school without fear. She still believes that kindness exists.\r\n\r\nThere is hope.\r\n\r\nA life-changing orbital decompression surgery, costing $20,000, could relieve the pressure around her eyes, protect her vision, improve her breathing, and give her the chance to live a safer, healthier, and more normal life.\r\n\r\nSadly, our family cannot afford this surgery on our own.\r\n\r\nThat is why I am humbly asking for your help.\r\n\r\nEvery donation, no matter the amount, brings my daughter one step closer to the life every child deserves—a life without constant pain, without fear, and without being judged simply because she was born different.\r\n\r\nFrom the bottom of my heart, thank you for taking the time to read our story.\r\n\r\nThank you for believing in my little girl.\r\n\r\nWith love,\r\n\r\nSusan","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/saves-susan/1784232676-8e23a5aa.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/saves-susan/1784232676-8e23a5aa.jpeg"],"raised":12980,"goal":20000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Anthee","words_of_support":[{"name":"Flavia Smith","amount":"$250","time":"8 minutes ago","message":"No child should ever have to go through this. Sending all my love and prayers to beautiful Anthee. ❤️"},{"name":"Michael T","amount":"$20","time":"15 minutes ago","message":"Your daughter is stronger than most adults I know. I hope this surgery gives her the future she deserves. God bless your family."},{"name":"Emily Williams","amount":"$100","time":"22 minutes ago","message":"Reading this brought me to tears. Praying that Anthee never loses her beautiful heart. ❤️🙏"},{"name":"Daniel Harris","amount":"$100","time":"34 minutes ago","message":"Every child deserves to feel accepted and loved. I hope many people come together to help Anthee."},{"name":"Jessica Moore","amount":"$50","time":"48 minutes ago","message":"Stay strong, Susan. Your daughter is absolutely precious, and brighter days are coming. ❤️"},{"name":"Christopher Allen","amount":"$30","time":"1 hour ago","message":"I can't imagine what your family has been through. Hoping this fundraiser reaches its goal very soon."},{"name":"Amanda Scott","amount":"$50","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Anthee, you are beautiful exactly as you are. Wishing you a successful surgery and a future filled with happiness. 💕"},{"name":"David Wilson","amount":"$50","time":"2 2 hours ago","message":"No mother should have to watch her child suffer like this. Keeping your family in my prayers. May God bless Anthee."}],"donations_count":"432","created_at":"2026-07-09T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"efc25d63-3bf6-4969-a450-4bb76527405d","slug":"help-jhonata","title":"Ayuda a Jhonata a conseguir prótesis de brazos","description":"Me llamo Samuel, y este es mi hijo Jhonata. 💔\n\nJhonata nació sin sus dos brazos después de graves complicaciones y presunta negligencia médica durante el parto. Lo que debía ser el día más feliz de nuestras vidas se convirtió en una tragedia: mi esposa no sobrevivió y nuestro hijo llegó al mundo sin sus brazos.\n\nDesde entonces, lo he criado solo. He aprendido a alimentarlo, vestirlo, bañarlo y cuidarlo con mis propias manos, mientras cargo con el dolor de haber perdido a mi esposa y veo a mi hijo enfrentar una vida tan difícil.\n\nJhonata es un niño fuerte, inteligente y lleno de amor. Ahora que está creciendo, empieza a darse cuenta de todo. Ve a otros niños correr, jugar, dibujar y abrazar, y me pregunta por qué él no tiene brazos como ellos. Cada vez que lo pregunta, se me rompe el alma.\n\nEl bullying en la escuela fue tan cruel que tuvimos que retirarlo. Otros niños se burlaban de él y lo hacían sentir menos. Ningún niño debería pasar por tanto dolor y humillación.\n\nSoy un padre humilde y trabajo todo lo que puedo, pero no alcanzo a pagar las prótesis de brazos que Jhonata necesita para tener más independencia, volver a la escuela, jugar y vivir con dignidad.\n\nNo estoy pidiendo lujos. Solo quiero que mi hijo tenga una oportunidad real de vivir como cualquier otro niño. Cualquier ayuda, por pequeña que sea, puede cambiarle la vida.\n\nAyúdame a darle a Jhonata las prótesis que necesita. Gracias por escuchar nuestra historia. 🙏💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-jhonata/1.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-jhonata/1.jpg"],"raised":12215,"goal":27000,"category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Samuel","location":"Chiapas, México","words_of_support":[{"name":"Robert Bailey","amount":"$500","time":"Hace 5 horas","message":"Dono con amor y esperanza. Que encuentres la fuerza para superar este momento difícil."},{"name":"Barbara Campbell","amount":"$300","time":"Hace un momento","message":"Toda nuestra familia te apoya. Tienes más gente de tu lado de la que crees."},{"name":"Evelyn Rodriguez","amount":"$25","time":"Hace 12 minutos","message":"Qué historia tan increíble. Muy agradecida de poder ayudar aunque sea un poco. Que Dios te bendiga."}],"donations_count":"244","created_at":"2026-06-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://rd-bfoundation.org/site/campaign-detail.html?id=efc25d63-3bf6-4969-a450-4bb76527405d"},{"id":"help-save-alexa","slug":"help-save-alexa","title":"Help save Alexa — support her fight against SCA3","description":"Hi, my name is Alexa, and I have a rare disease called SCA3 (Spinocerebellar Ataxia Type 3). It affects all movement, especially voluntary functions such as speaking, walking, swallowing, seeing, and many others. It is a progressive disease. My symptoms began in 2012, and they have continued to worsen over the years.\n\nI am originally from the United Kingdom and currently live in the United States. I moved here six years ago with my ex-husband and my daughter. Since October 2024, I have had no contact with my daughter whatsoever. There was no mediation from social services. I met the social worker responsible for her case only three times, and it took a tremendous amount of effort to make even those meetings happen. I do not know him well enough to understand why he has not done his job. As a result, I have been completely cut off from my daughter for more than a year and a half, with no way to communicate with her or know how she is doing.\n\nDue to several traumatic events that occurred last year, which I have explained in my videos, my health has been severely affected. Before all of this, I was able to go out by myself, cook, and live an almost normal life.\n\nNow, I need more support. My caregivers only have enough time to prepare meals and help with basic household tasks. I am currently applying for additional caregiving hours for the third time so that I can leave my home accompanied by a helper.\n\nLast year, I became extremely debilitated. Despite everything I was going through emotionally, I also had to be hospitalized multiple times due to complications related to my disease.\n\nI have many expenses, including medical bills, medications, nutritional supplements, rent, and household utilities. I would also like to travel to visit my family in the United Kingdom, but airfare is very expensive, and I would need a caregiver to accompany me on the trip.\n\nI also need a life. Right now, I am only surviving. I live alone in my apartment and am completely isolated from the world—not because I choose to be. This is not loneliness; it is isolation. And isolation has a devastating impact on the brain and emotional well-being.\n\nI need glasses because my eyesight has deteriorated significantly, and I can no longer read comfortably. I also need to purchase a computer because managing my life through a cellphone has become increasingly difficult. My hands shake due to parkinsonism, which is another symptom I deal with daily.\n\nThere is currently no cure and no effective treatment for my disease.\n\nI have no support network in the United States. Once or twice a year, an acquaintance may come to visit. People are busy living their own lives, which is understandable. But I, too, need some form of social connection and human interaction.\n\nToday, I am humbly asking for your support. Any donation, no matter how small, will make a meaningful difference in my life.\n\nI will be forever grateful for your kindness and generosity.\n\nPlease help me find some relief, peace, and dignity during this difficult journey.\n\nThank you from the bottom of my heart.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlexa","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-save-alexa/1.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-save-alexa/1.jpeg"],"raised":11548,"goal":15000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Alexandra Beck","words_of_support":[{"name":"Joe Frings","amount":"$500","time":"1 hour","message":"Sending love and encouragement. Good luck guys"},{"name":"James Brown","amount":"$100","time":"6 hours","message":"I made a prayer for Alexa. May God save"},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"21 hours","message":"I set my part, it's painful to see this woman going through this."},{"name":"Will Miller","amount":"$250","time":"1 day","message":"Money raised from Leni's raffle run by the amazing We Brought Beer in Tooting Market!"},{"name":"Piter Garcia","amount":"$50","time":"6 days","message":"If we all help a little, we can save her from this."},{"name":"United Lodge of Prudednce No.83","amount":"$50","time":"8 days","message":"On behalf of our Worshipful Master, Steve Pallett, and all the Brethren of the Lodge, we wish you well"},{"name":"Vander Anderson","amount":"$50","time":"1 month","message":"God bless you little one"},{"name":"Udson Estrella","amount":"$50","time":"2 months","message":"Sending love from Logan (Kido) and family."}],"donations_count":"536","created_at":"2026-03-03T00:00:00-03:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"0e272eba-113d-493f-9963-6d8ea7d9aeb3","slug":"help-save-nora","title":"Urgent Help Needed for Nora’s Aggressive Facial Cancer","description":"This first photo was taken a few months ago, when my mother was still healthy, smiling, and taking care of us like she always did. The second photo… is what she looks like now. 💔\n\nMy name is Christopher, and I’m writing this from Uganda with a pain I can’t even explain. I am the oldest son of my mother, Nora, and I feel like I am watching her disappear in front of me… and I can’t do anything to stop it.\n\nIt started as something small. Just a wound on her face that we thought would heal. But it didn’t. It kept growing. Slowly at first… and then faster and faster, until in a couple months it became something we could no longer ignore.\n\nNow, that cancer is eating away at her face.\n\nThe pain she feels every single day is unbearable. The wound is open, it bleeds constantly, and we don’t even have proper medical supplies to clean it. We use old cloths just to try and help her. Sometimes the smell and the infection get worse, and she just sits there… suffering in silence.\n\nShe can no longer eat properly. Even trying to swallow causes her extreme pain. Most days, she barely eats anything at all. Her body is getting weaker, thinner… and I can see that she is slowly losing the strength to keep fighting.\n\nThere are moments when she tries to speak, but she can’t. The tumor has taken so much from her already. She spends most of her time lying down, unable to move, unable to live the life she once had.\n\nMy mother is a single mother of seven children. After my father passed away, she carried everything on her own. She worked every day just to make sure we had something to eat. She was strong for all of us. She was everything.\n\nAnd now… she is the one who needs us.\n\nWe live in very poor conditions here in Uganda. We don’t have access to proper healthcare, and we have no money for treatment. There are days when we don’t even have food. We are completely alone in this.\n\nWe recently went to a hospital, and the doctors told us the truth we were afraid to hear. The cancer is aggressive and spreading fast. Without urgent surgery to remove the tumor, she may not survive.\n\nThere is a chance to save her… but we cannot afford it.\n\nThe surgery she needs is not only to remove the cancer, but also to reconstruct her face so she can live without this constant pain and suffering. But for us, it is impossible to pay for it alone.\n\nEvery day I wake up scared that it might be the day I lose my mother. Every day I see her getting worse. And every day, I feel more helpless.\n\nPlease… if you are reading this, I am begging you. Don’t look away.\n\nAny donation, no matter how small, can help save my mother’s life. The money will go toward her surgery, medical care, medication, and basic needs for our family while we fight to keep her alive.\n\nI don’t want to lose my mother. We still need her.\n\nPlease help us save her. Donate now. 💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-save-nora/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-save-nora/1.png"],"raised":10720,"goal":20000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Christopher","location":"Uganda","words_of_support":[{"name":"Brandon Edwards","amount":"$50","time":"Recent donation","message":"Wishing you all the strength and courage you need. You are not alone in this journey. ❤️"},{"name":"Linda Young","amount":"$100","time":"3 hours ago","message":"Your story moved us deeply. We hope this small contribution helps make a difference."},{"name":"Melissa Lee","amount":"$500","time":"3 days ago","message":"Thank you for sharing your story. We are honored to be part of your journey. Stay strong!"}],"donations_count":"214","created_at":"2026-04-23T15:18:53.259488+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://brightfuturefoundations.com/campaign-detail?id=0e272eba-113d-493f-9963-6d8ea7d9aeb3"},{"id":"lumani-impact-lumora-joel","slug":"joel","title":"Mi hijo Joel Pérez tiene solo 7 años y lucha contra una enfermedad renal. Solo les pido una oportunidad para seguir cuidándolo.","description":"Mi nombre es Lucía Pérez, y nunca imaginé que algún día tendría que pedir ayuda públicamente para salvar a mi hijo.\n\nMi hijo, Joel Pérez, tiene apenas 7 años y padece una enfermedad en los riñones. Cada día veo a un niño tan pequeño soportar un dolor que ningún niño debería conocer. Entre consultas médicas, exámenes, medicamentos y noches sin dormir, mi único deseo es poder aliviar su sufrimiento.\n\nCuando el padre de Joel supo de la enfermedad de nuestro hijo, decidió abandonarnos. Desde entonces, solo estamos mi pequeño y yo enfrentando esta dura batalla. No tengo a nadie que me ayude y no puedo dejarlo solo ni un solo momento. Él depende completamente de mí para llevarlo a sus consultas, realizar sus estudios, darle sus medicamentos y acompañarlo cuando el dolor se vuelve insoportable.\n\nDebido a que debo cuidarlo las 24 horas del día, no puedo trabajar. Sin un ingreso económico, cada día se ha convertido en una lucha para conseguir sus medicamentos, pagar los exámenes médicos y cubrir las necesidades más básicas de nuestro hogar. Muchas veces me veo obligada a elegir entre comprar un medicamento para aliviar su dolor o poner comida en nuestra mesa.\n\nJoel es un niño noble, cariñoso y lleno de sueños. Debería estar jugando, corriendo y disfrutando de su infancia, pero en lugar de eso pasa gran parte de su vida entre hospitales, consultas y tratamientos. A pesar del dolor que siente, todavía encuentra fuerzas para sonreír y preguntarme cuándo podrá volver a jugar como los demás niños. Esas preguntas rompen mi corazón.\n\nComo madre, el dolor más grande es no poder darle todo lo que necesita. Jamás imaginé que tendría que pedir ayuda a personas que no conozco, pero hoy dejo mi orgullo de lado porque la vida y la salud de mi hijo son mucho más importantes que cualquier otra cosa.\n\nPor eso les pido, con todo mi corazón, que si pueden hacer una donación, sin importar el monto, estarán cambiando nuestras vidas. Su ayuda nos permitirá comprar medicamentos, realizar los exámenes que Joel necesita, continuar con su tratamiento y cubrir las necesidades básicas de nuestro hogar mientras sigo dedicando todo mi tiempo a cuidarlo.\n\nY si no pueden donar, les ruego que compartan nuestra historia. Tal vez llegue a alguien que pueda darnos la esperanza que tanto necesitamos.\n\nEn nombre de mi pequeño Joel Pérez, gracias por leer nuestra historia, por cada oración, por cada mensaje de apoyo y por cualquier ayuda que puedan brindarnos. Que Dios bendiga profundamente a cada persona que decida extendernos su mano en este momento tan difícil.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/joel/IMG_5256.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/joel/IMG_5256.jpg","uploads/campaigns/joel/IMG_5255.jpg"],"raised":10627,"goal":20000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":false,"organizer":"Joel Pérez","location":"Ubicación no especificada","words_of_support":[{"name":"María González","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 8 minutos","message":"Acabo de hacer mi donación. Espero de todo corazón que Joel pueda recibir los medicamentos que tanto necesita. Dios los bendiga. ❤️"},{"name":"Carlos Ramírez","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 14 minutos","message":"Ningún niño debería pasar por tanto dolor. Ya envié mi ayuda. Mucha fuerza para Joel y para su mamá."},{"name":"Ana Rodríguez","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 21 minutos","message":"😢 Soy mamá y esta historia me hizo llorar. Espero que más personas puedan ayudar a esta hermosa familia."},{"name":"José Martínez","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 29 minutos","message":"❤️ Donado. Que Dios acompañe a Joel en cada etapa de su tratamiento. Nunca pierdan la esperanza."},{"name":"Laura Herrera","amount":"$20","time":"Hace 36 minutos","message":"🙏 Compartido con toda mi familia. Ojalá esta campaña llegue a miles de personas."},{"name":"Miguel Torres","amount":"$250","time":"Hace 45 minutos","message":"Acabo de hacer mi aporte. Espero que puedan cubrir los gastos médicos y las necesidades básicas de su hogar."},{"name":"Patricia Mendoza","amount":"$30","time":"Hace 52 minutos","message":"Muchísima fuerza, Lucía. Eres una madre admirable y Joel tiene mucha suerte de tenerte."},{"name":"Fernando López","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Ya colaboré. Rezo para que Joel pueda vivir una infancia sin tanto sufrimiento."}],"donations_count":"434","created_at":"2026-06-11T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://lumani-impact.org/joel/"},{"id":"af255a5d-518e-406f-a321-e3cb455b43fb","slug":"help-will-survive","title":"Help Will Survive Aggressive Gastrointestinal Cancer","description":"My name is Will Hudson, and I never thought I’d be here begging strangers for help just to stay alive.\n\nI’m fighting a very aggressive gastrointestinal cancer that’s destroying me from the inside. It’s cruel. I can barely eat anymore. Every time I try to swallow, it feels like fire going down my throat and most of the time the food just comes back up. I’m losing weight so fast, getting weaker every single day, and the pain in my stomach and intestines never stops.\n\nI feel like I’m slowly fading away. Some days I don’t even have the strength to stand up. I’m exhausted, always hungry, scared, and I feel my body giving up.\n\nThe doctors say I need urgent chemotherapy and treatment right away, otherwise the cancer will spread more and I won’t survive. But I have no money. I’m completely alone in this fight.\n\nI’m not asking for anything fancy. I just want a real chance to keep living.\n\nAny donation, even if it’s only $25 or $100, can help me get the treatment I need.\n\nPlease… don’t scroll past this. I’m running out of time. Your help could mean the difference between life and death for me.\n\nIf you can’t donate, please share my story or pray for me.\n\nThank you, and God bless you for caring about someone who’s fighting to survive. 💔🙏","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-will-survive/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-will-survive/1.png","uploads/campaigns/help-will-survive/2.jpg","uploads/campaigns/help-will-survive/3.png"],"raised":9890,"goal":25000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"organizer":"Will Hudson","location":"Pine Bluff, Arkansas","words_of_support":[{"name":"Barbara Lee","amount":"$25","time":"Recent donation","message":"Wishing you all the strength and courage you need. You are not alone in this journey. ❤️"},{"name":"Anonymous","amount":"$500","time":"2 days ago","message":"Your story moved us deeply. We hope this small contribution helps make a difference."},{"name":"Patricia Carter","amount":"$100","time":"25 minutes ago","message":"Thank you for sharing your story. We are honored to be part of your journey. Stay strong!"}],"donations_count":"197","created_at":"2026-06-08T00:37:14.945012+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://brightfuturefoundations.com/campaign-detail?id=af255a5d-518e-406f-a321-e3cb455b43fb"},{"id":"697a8f83-b5df-430c-9911-a3804a94b0d0","slug":"help-joyce-jaw-cancer","title":"Help Joyce Receive Her Second Jaw Cancer Surgery","description":"My name is Joyce, and I am writing from a small town outside Houston, Texas, with a fear that never leaves my mind anymore. I never imagined I would be asking strangers for help just to stay alive, but I truly do not know what else to do.\n\nA couple of years ago, I was diagnosed with cancer in my jaw. Doctors initially believed they had removed it. I went through surgery, pain, medication and months of recovery, holding onto the hope that my life would finally return to normal.\n\nThen the pain slowly returned. My jaw began swelling more each week. I prayed that it was only inflammation or an infection, but the cancer had come back. This time, doctors told me it was spreading toward my brain.\n\nThe pressure and pain in my face can be unbearable. Eating has become difficult, talking exhausts me, and some mornings I wake up dizzy and weak. The swelling continues to grow, and I barely recognize myself in the mirror.\n\nAfter years of appointments, scans, medication and treatment, I am financially exhausted. I have tried to continue working through the pain, but my body is reaching a point where it cannot keep going like this.\n\nDoctors say I need urgent treatment and another major surgery to have a chance of stopping the cancer before it spreads further. Donations will help cover surgery, cancer treatment, imaging scans, hospital visits, medication, pain management, transportation and basic living expenses during recovery.\n\nI am scared of what will happen if I cannot afford treatment in time, but I am still holding onto hope. Any donation can make a real difference. If you cannot donate, sharing my story or keeping me in your prayers means more than you know.\n\nPlease help me keep fighting. 💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-joyce-jaw-cancer/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-joyce-jaw-cancer/1.png"],"raised":8595,"goal":18155,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Joyce","location":"Texas, United States","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jessica Green","amount":"$100","time":"12 minutes ago","message":"Donating with love and hope. May you find the strength to get through this difficult time."},{"name":"Tyler Hill","amount":"$50","time":"5 minutes ago","message":"Our whole family is rooting for you. You have more people in your corner than you know."},{"name":"Laura Lee","amount":"$25","time":"2 minutes ago","message":"What an incredible story. So grateful to be able to help in a small way. God bless you."}],"donations_count":"171","created_at":"2026-05-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://rd-bfoundation.org/site/campaign-detail.html?id=697a8f83-b5df-430c-9911-a3804a94b0d0"},{"id":"cd543f0f-a40e-4491-8d76-ef26a5d6fe30","slug":"ayuda-patricia","title":"Ayuda a Patricia con morfina y tratamiento para su hijo","description":"Hola, mi nombre es Patricia, y escribo esto con el corazón en la mano porque estoy pasando por un dolor que ya no sé cómo soportar.\n\nSoy madre, una mujer humilde y trabajadora, y estoy luchando contra un cáncer de tiroides con metástasis pulmonar. Esta enfermedad me está consumiendo poco a poco, y cada día despierto con miedo de no tener fuerzas para seguir.\n\nEl dolor es insoportable. Me duele el pecho y el cuerpo, me falta el aire y hay momentos en los que el sufrimiento es tan fuerte que me desmayo. Necesito aplicarme doce ampollas de morfina al día para resistir, pero a veces el dolor parece más fuerte que la medicina.\n\nLlevo días sin poder aplicarme la morfina porque no tengo dinero para comprarla. Han sido días de llanto, desesperación y oraciones, porque no sé qué más hacer.\n\nComo si mi sufrimiento no fuera suficiente, mi hijo mayor también está enfermo. Sufrió una infección grave en la retina del ojo izquierdo y perdió la visión de ese lado. El médico advirtió que podrían quedar secuelas. Como madre, escuchar eso me destruyó.\n\nEstoy luchando contra el cáncer y al mismo tiempo veo sufrir a mi hijo sin poder darle todo lo que necesita. Me duele el cuerpo, pero también me duele el alma.\n\nNecesito ayuda para comprar morfina y otras medicinas, pagar consultas y tratamientos, y ayudar a mi hijo con el cuidado de su ojo.\n\nCualquier donación puede aliviar mi dolor y darme fuerzas para seguir luchando. Si no puedes donar, comparte nuestra historia y deja una oración por mí y por mi hijo. Dios les bendiga de todo corazón. 🙏💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ayuda-patricia/1.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/ayuda-patricia/1.jpg"],"raised":6800,"goal":30000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Patricia Panta","location":"Piura, Perú","words_of_support":[{"name":"Nicole Howard","amount":"$50","time":"Hace 1 hora","message":"Gracias por compartir tu historia. Es un honor ser parte de tu camino. ¡Mantente fuerte!"},{"name":"Mark Moore","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Eres una inspiración. Sigue luchando — vienen días mejores. Enviamos oraciones desde nuestra familia."},{"name":"Tyler Edwards","amount":"$300","time":"Hace 25 minutos","message":"Vimos tu campaña y no pudimos seguir de largo. Mereces todo el apoyo del mundo."}],"donations_count":"136","created_at":"2026-06-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://rd-bfoundation.org/site/campaign-detail.html?id=cd543f0f-a40e-4491-8d76-ef26a5d6fe30"},{"id":"0aa1871a-af72-4775-80af-7d7399835663","slug":"akin","title":"Akin Has 6 Months to Live — Be His Only Hope","description":"Right now, a young boy named Akin is fighting for his life — completely alone.\n\nAkin was abandoned by his parents. He has no family to hold his hand, protect him, or fight beside him. We are the only ones he has left.\n\nAkin is suffering from an extremely aggressive cancer in his eye. The disease has already spread to his brain and other organs, and doctors have given him just six months to live.\n\nHe is only a child, but he is already facing death alone. Every day the tumor grows, his pain gets worse, and without immediate care he may not survive long enough to have a future.\n\nOur emergency funds are gone, and time is slipping away. Goal 1 brought him some pain relief, but Goal 2 will fund the urgent scans and laboratory work doctors need to understand how far the cancer has spread.\n\nWe urgently need $2,520 more to unlock those tests. Without the scans, treatment cannot move forward. The full fight still needs $20,000, but this next step cannot wait.\n\nThis is not about tomorrow. This is about giving Akin a chance to live right now. Every donation could be the reason he survives another day.\n\nGoal 1 — Pain Relief ($4,000): Funded. Essential medication has begun easing Akin's pain.\n\nGoal 2 — Urgent Tests ($9,000): Still blocked. Scans and labs must map the cancer before treatment can proceed.\n\nGoal 3 — Start Treatment ($14,000): Early-stage cancer care can begin once doctors can see what they are fighting.\n\nGoal 4 — Full Fight ($20,000): Aggressive treatment to give Akin a real chance at survival.\n\nPlease help us save Akin. If you cannot donate today, sharing his story can still bring the person who can.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/akin/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/akin/1.webp","uploads/campaigns/akin/2.webp","uploads/campaigns/akin/3.webp"],"video_url":"uploads/campaigns/akin/akin-situation.mp4","video_poster":"uploads/campaigns/akin/3.webp","video_label":"Akin's Story","video_heading":"See Akin's Real Situation","video_description":"This video shows the severity of Akin's condition. Doctors gave him just six months to live, and he needs help right now.","video_warning":"This video contains real footage of Akin's condition.","raised":6480,"goal":20000,"category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Africa","words_of_support":[{"name":"Rebecca T.","amount":"$50","time":"2 hours ago","message":"I can't imagine what Akin is going through. Stay strong, little one! ❤️🙏"},{"name":"James R.","amount":"$100","time":"3 hours ago","message":"No child should suffer like this. Donated and shared with everyone I know."},{"name":"Lauren C.","amount":"$25","time":"5 hours ago","message":"Donated what I could. Please share this — Akin needs us!"}],"donations_count":"174","created_at":"2026-08-21T14:21:08+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://onehopefoundation.online/akin"},{"id":"3d6fa76c-04b1-4058-bb20-58c5db90fe24","slug":"help-noah","title":"Help Noah Afford Scleral Lenses and Eye Surgery","description":"My name is Noah Brooks, and I am asking for help because I am scared of losing the little vision I have left.\n\nWhen I was a child, I survived Stevens-Johnson Syndrome, a rare and life-threatening disease that almost took my life. I survived, but it severely damaged my eyes and left me with very limited vision. I have only one functioning eye left; the other is badly damaged.\n\nSimple things other people do without thinking are difficult for me. Reading, walking outside, recognizing faces, cooking, working, getting around safely and living independently all require enormous effort.\n\nThis has also caused severe anxiety and depression. The fear of losing more vision, the frustration of depending on others and the loneliness of living in darkness have taken a heavy toll on my mental health.\n\nI have finally found a specialist in New York who may be able to help. I urgently need specialized scleral lenses that could improve my vision and reduce the more than twenty eye drops I use each day, as well as complex surgery on my only functioning eye.\n\nMy insurance will not cover these treatments, and the cost reaches six figures. Follow-up appointments are required every six weeks, and I cannot afford them alone. I have held onto the dream of seeing better for 33 years, but every time I get close, it is pulled away again.\n\nI am not asking for luxury. I am asking for the chance to see better, live with greater independence and stop feeling so alone in this fight.\n\nPlease help me access the surgery and specialized lenses I need. Any donation brings me one step closer to protecting my remaining vision. If you cannot donate, sharing my story or saying a prayer can still help. 🙏💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-noah/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-noah/1.png","uploads/campaigns/help-noah/2.png"],"raised":5435,"goal":20000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Noah Brooks","location":"Williamsport, Pennsylvania","words_of_support":[{"name":"Amanda Mitchell","amount":"$50","time":"3 hours ago","message":"We saw your campaign and couldn't scroll past. You deserve all the support in the world."},{"name":"Samantha Martinez","amount":"$500","time":"1 day ago","message":"Donating with love and hope. May you find the strength to get through this difficult time."},{"name":"Amelia Ramirez","amount":"$1,000","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Our whole family is rooting for you. You have more people in your corner than you know."}],"donations_count":"108","created_at":"2026-07-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://rd-bfoundation.org/site/campaign-detail.html?id=3d6fa76c-04b1-4058-bb20-58c5db90fe24"},{"id":"abcf5122-e305-4691-ad35-1ad91f174ffb","slug":"ayuda-alejandro","title":"Ayuda a Carmen a salvar a su hijo Alejandro","description":"Mi nombre es Carmen, y escribo esto con el corazón destrozado por mi hijo Alejandro.\n\nSoy madre soltera y viuda. Somos una familia humilde, y desde hace tiempo mi vida se convirtió en cuidar a mi hijo día y noche mientras lo veo sufrir en una cama sin poder darle todo lo que necesita.\n\nAlejandro está muy enfermo. Vive postrado, con dolores fuertes, heridas abiertas en las piernas y una debilidad que no le permite levantarse ni llevar una vida normal. No puede caminar, bañarse, ir al baño o salir sin ayuda. Depende de mí para casi todo.\n\nHay días en los que llora desesperadamente por el dolor. A veces queda dormido de tanto sufrir, y yo permanezco a su lado sintiendo que se me rompe el alma porque soy su madre y no tengo cómo aliviarlo.\n\nHe ido al hospital, pedido ayuda y buscado atención, pero muchas veces nos hacen esperar. Mientras tanto, mi hijo sigue en casa con dolor y sin la atención urgente que necesita.\n\nNo puedo trabajar porque no puedo dejarlo solo. Tengo que cuidarlo, cambiarlo, limpiarlo, darle sus medicinas y estar pendiente de él todo el día. Ya no tengo dinero para pañales, medicamentos, alcohol, curaciones, transporte o un médico que pueda visitarlo.\n\nSus heridas, su dolor y su debilidad necesitan atención urgente antes de que sea demasiado tarde. Las donaciones ayudarán a comprar pañales, medicinas, materiales de curación, atención médica, terapia y todo lo que Alejandro necesita para seguir luchando.\n\nCualquier donación puede ayudarnos muchísimo. Si no puedes donar, comparte su historia y deja una oración por mi hijo. 🙏💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ayuda-alejandro/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/ayuda-alejandro/1.png","uploads/campaigns/ayuda-alejandro/2.png"],"raised":5390,"goal":25000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Carmen González","location":"Piura, Perú","words_of_support":[{"name":"George Murphy","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 2 horas","message":"Vimos tu campaña y no pudimos seguir de largo. Mereces todo el apoyo del mundo."},{"name":"Karen Lewis","amount":"$1,000","time":"Hace 25 minutos","message":"Dono con amor y esperanza. Que encuentres la fuerza para superar este momento difícil."},{"name":"Steven Hill","amount":"$500","time":"Hace 3 días","message":"Toda nuestra familia te apoya. Tienes más gente de tu lado de la que crees."}],"donations_count":"107","created_at":"2026-07-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://rd-bfoundation.org/site/campaign-detail.html?id=abcf5122-e305-4691-ad35-1ad91f174ffb"},{"id":"b8af131b-7d0b-49d7-8cac-b6434314f323","slug":"ayuda-gael","title":"Ayuda a Gael a luchar contra un cáncer agresivo","description":"Mi nombre es Mariana, y escribo esto con el corazón destrozado por mi bebé Gael.\n\nGael tiene solo 6 meses. Debería estar creciendo, sonriendo, moviendo sus manitos y descubriendo el mundo en mis brazos. El día que nació fue el momento más feliz de mi vida.\n\nPocos meses después recibimos una noticia que nos destruyó. Mi bebé fue diagnosticado con neuroblastoma, un cáncer agresivo que afecta a niños pequeños y puede avanzar muy rápido. Desde ese día vivimos con miedo, dolor y la angustia de no saber si podremos salvarlo.\n\nGael es tan pequeño que no puede decir dónde le duele. Solo llora, se cansa, se debilita y me mira como si pidiera ayuda. Hay momentos en los que lo abrazo y me rompo por dentro porque soy su mamá y no puedo quitarle el sufrimiento.\n\nÉl debería estar durmiendo tranquilo y sintiéndose seguro. En cambio, necesita médicos, exámenes, medicamentos, hospitalización, tratamiento y una cirugía urgente para luchar contra el cáncer.\n\nLos médicos nos explicaron que, si no recibe tratamiento rápido, la enfermedad puede seguir avanzando y poner su vida en peligro en pocos meses.\n\nSomos una familia humilde y no estábamos preparados para esto. No tenemos dinero para pagar todo lo que necesita, y cada día que pasa sin tratamiento sentimos que el tiempo se acaba.\n\nCualquier donación puede ayudarnos con su cirugía, medicamentos, exámenes, hospital, transporte y tratamiento urgente. Si no puedes donar, comparte su historia y deja una oración por Gael. 🙏💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ayuda-gael/1.png","images":["uploads/campaigns/ayuda-gael/1.png","uploads/campaigns/ayuda-gael/2.png"],"raised":5060,"goal":30000,"category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Mariana Torres","location":"Puebla, México","words_of_support":[{"name":"Nicole Parker","amount":"$1,000","time":"Donación mayor","message":"Te deseo toda la fuerza y el coraje que necesitas. No estás solo en este camino. ❤️"},{"name":"Linda Davis","amount":"$25","time":"Hace 12 minutos","message":"Tu historia nos conmovió profundamente. Esperamos que esta contribución ayude a marcar la diferencia."},{"name":"Michael Young","amount":"$300","time":"Hace 1 día","message":"Gracias por compartir tu historia. Es un honor ser parte de tu camino. ¡Mantente fuerte!"}],"donations_count":"101","created_at":"2026-07-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://brightfuturefoundations.com/campaign-detail?id=b8af131b-7d0b-49d7-8cac-b6434314f323","alternate_source_url":"https://brightfuturesfoundations.org/campaigns/ayuda-a-gael-a-luchar-contra-el-cancer"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-amelia","slug":"help-amelia","title":"Help Amelia Fight Cancer for Her Two Little Girls","description":"My name is Amelia Jones. I am 23 years old, and I am a single mother to two little girls who depend entirely on me.\n\nRecently, my life changed in an instant when I found out that I have cancer.\n\nDoctors believe it is a low-grade fibromyxoid sarcoma. I now face radiation, surgery, scans, biopsies and possibly more treatment in the months ahead.\n\nBecause of my illness, I had to stop working. At the same time, I still have two young daughters to feed, house and care for while facing the growing costs of medical appointments, treatment, surgery, transportation and recovery.\n\nTheir father is not present in their lives.\n\nI am all they have.\n\nThe hardest part of this battle is not the pain, the hospital visits or even the financial stress. It is the fear that I may not be here to watch my daughters grow up.\n\nI am terrified of dying and leaving my little girls without their mother.\n\nI want more birthdays with them. More bedtime hugs. More school mornings. More years to love them, protect them and be their mom.\n\nAny donation will help me cover our basic living expenses and the costs of treatment while I am unable to work.\n\nIf you cannot donate, please share my story or keep my family in your prayers.\n\nI am not only fighting cancer. I am fighting for the chance to stay alive and raise my two little girls. ❤️","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-amelia/1.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-amelia/1.jpeg"],"raised":3920,"goal":15000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Amelia Jones","location":"United States","words_of_support":[{"name":"Emily Carter","amount":"$100","time":"1 hour ago","message":"Praying for you and your beautiful girls, Amelia. Stay strong. ❤️"},{"name":"Jessica Morgan","amount":"$50","time":"3 hours ago","message":"You are such a strong mama. Sending love, prayers, and strength to your family. 🙏❤️"},{"name":"Ashley Evans","amount":"$1,000","time":"Top donation","message":"Donated and shared. I hope this helps even a little. Stay strong! ❤️"}],"donations_count":"78","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://peacetrailfoundation.org/help-amelia/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-george","slug":"help-george","title":"Help George Continue His Cancer Treatment and Get a Prosthetic Arm","description":"My name is George Taylor, and I am fighting a rare type of cancer that has completely changed my life.\n\nAfter my arm became severely swollen, I went to the hospital and was diagnosed with alveolar soft-part sarcoma. The cancer affected my arm so severely that I had to undergo an amputation.\n\nI am still receiving cancer treatment, but I lost my health insurance and I am unable to work the way I used to. My mother is the person standing by my side, but the cost of treatment, medications, medical tests, transportation and everyday expenses has become more than we can afford alone.\n\nI am raising funds to continue my cancer treatment and to get a prosthetic arm, which could help me regain some of my independence and hopefully allow me to return to work and rebuild my life in the future.\n\nAny donation, no matter the amount, can make a real difference. If you are unable to donate, please consider sharing my fundraiser with others. ❤️\n\nThank you for helping me continue this fight.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-george/1.jpeg","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-george/1.jpeg"],"raised":3920,"goal":15000,"category":"health","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":false,"organizer":"George Taylor","location":"United States","words_of_support":[{"name":"Jane Cotta","amount":"$250","time":"1 hour ago","message":"George's story is heartbreaking. I hope as many people as possible can come together to support him through his treatment and help him get the prosthetic arm he needs. Please donate or share if you can."},{"name":"Julian Brown","amount":"$20","time":"12 hours ago","message":"Wishing George and his mum strength during such a difficult time. Every donation and every share can help this campaign reach more people."},{"name":"Emily Johnson","amount":"$100","time":"1 day ago","message":"George has already been through so much. If you're able to help, please consider supporting his fundraiser. Even simply sharing his story can make a difference."}],"donations_count":"78","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://brighthandsfoundation.org/help-george/"},{"id":"lumani-impact-help-adrieli","slug":"help-adrieli","title":"Help Adrieli Access Ongoing Epidermolysis Bullosa Care","description":"Adrieli lives in the countryside and has Epidermolysis Bullosa, a rare condition that makes her skin extremely fragile and requires careful daily treatment. Her family is raising funds for the specialized care and supplies she needs throughout the month.\n\nSupport can help cover non-stick dressings, medical visits, medication, nutrition, supplements, transportation and protective skin care. Consistent access to these essentials can make her daily routine safer and more comfortable.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/healing.webp|Specialized dressings are part of Adrieli's ongoing care.\n\nThe supplied monthly estimate is $93,550: $86,800 for specialized dressings, $3,000 for medical visits and tests, $1,000 for gastroenterology visits, $750 for dermatology visits, $600 for supplements and medication, $600 for nutrition support, $500 for transportation and related expenses, and $300 for moisturizers and skin care.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/vitamins.webp|Nutrition and supplements support Adrieli's treatment plan.\n\nEvery contribution can help Adrieli's family maintain the care routine recommended for her condition. If you can, support Adrieli's ongoing care today.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/1.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/2.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/3.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/4.webp"],"video_player":"adrieli","video_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/adrieli-story.mp4","video_poster":"uploads/campaigns/help-adrieli/video-poster.jpg","video_label":"Adrieli's Story","video_heading":"Hear Adrieli's Story","video_description":"Watch Adrieli explain why consistent treatment and specialized supplies matter to her daily care.","video_warning":"This video discusses Adrieli's medical condition and treatment needs.","raised":1005.73,"goal":93550,"currency":"USD","category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Brazil","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"34","created_at":"2026-07-01T00:00:00Z","stripe_account_id":"bhf"},{"id":"b1d2dc55-b0ad-4ce1-aff9-d68b712cff3f","slug":"ayuda-ollie","title":"Ayuda a Ollie a luchar contra su tumor cerebral","description":"Mi nombre es Katherine Miller y estoy pidiendo ayuda para mi perro, Ollie.\n\nOllie es mi bebé, mi mejor amigo y quien ha estado a mi lado durante años. Ha dormido cerca de mí, me ha seguido por toda la casa, me ha consolado cuando lloraba y me ha dado su amor en momentos en los que me sentía completamente sola.\n\nPero ahora estoy viendo cómo sufre, y eso me está destrozando.\n\nTodo comenzó con pequeños cambios. Ollie parecía cansado, confundido y ya no era él mismo. Entonces, un día, su cuerpo comenzó a temblar repentinamente. Se puso débil, asustado y desorientado, y yo me quedé paralizada porque no entendía qué estaba ocurriendo. Lo sostuve entre mis brazos mientras lloraba, repetía su nombre y le rogaba que se quedara conmigo.\n\nDesde entonces, ha estado sufriendo convulsiones y episodios similares a derrames cerebrales. En un momento está aquí conmigo y, al siguiente, su cuerpo comienza a temblar de manera incontrolable, su mirada se pierde, apenas puede controlar sus movimientos y yo me siento impotente viendo a mi bebé sufrir frente a mí.\n\nCada vez que sucede, pienso que voy a perderlo.\n\nYa he gastado todo lo que tenía tratando de descubrir qué le ocurría. Consultas veterinarias, pruebas, atención de emergencia y exámenes: hice todo lo que pude porque no podía quedarme de brazos cruzados viendo cómo empeoraba.\n\nEl veterinario me dijo que Ollie tiene un tumor cerebral y que necesita tratamiento urgente. Esto no puede esperar. Cada convulsión somete su cuerpo a más estrés y podría causarle más daño cerebral.\n\nEl veterinario también le recetó fenobarbital para ayudar a controlar las convulsiones, pero el costo del medicamento, las consultas de seguimiento, los exámenes y el tratamiento es más de lo que puedo pagar por mi cuenta.\n\nSi Ollie no recibe pronto la atención que necesita, los episodios podrían volverse más frecuentes, más violentos y más difíciles de superar para su cuerpo. Podría perder aún más el control, debilitarse, dejar de comer, tener dificultades para caminar o sufrir una convulsión tan grave que quizá no vuelva a despertar.\n\nMe duele muchísimo saber que, después de tantos años amándome incondicionalmente, el dinero podría ser la razón por la que no pueda salvarlo.\n\nNo estoy preparada para perder a mi mejor amigo. Por favor, ayúdenme a salvar a Ollie. 🙏🐾💔","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/ayuda-ollie/1.jpg","images":["uploads/campaigns/ayuda-ollie/1.jpg","uploads/campaigns/ayuda-ollie/2.jpg","uploads/campaigns/ayuda-ollie/3.jpg"],"raised":950,"goal":5000,"category":"animals","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":true,"organizer":"Katherine Miller","location":"Kentucky, United States","words_of_support":[{"name":"Donald Williams","amount":"$50","time":"Donación reciente","message":"Te deseo toda la fuerza y el coraje que necesitas. No estás solo en este camino. ❤️"},{"name":"Thomas Nelson","amount":"$300","time":"Donación mayor","message":"Tu historia nos conmovió profundamente. Esperamos que esta pequeña contribución ayude a marcar la diferencia."},{"name":"John Young","amount":"$100","time":"Hace 3 días","message":"Gracias por compartir tu historia. Es un honor ser parte de tu camino. ¡Mantente fuerte!"}],"donations_count":"19","created_at":"2026-07-30T16:28:54.352862+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://brightfuturefoundations.com/campaign-detail?id=b1d2dc55-b0ad-4ce1-aff9-d68b712cff3f"},{"id":"529c46f9-db22-41b5-ad44-092353ecfcc1","slug":"help-arielle","title":"A Desperate Girl — Arielle Feels Pain Even When the Wind Touches Her Skin","description":"Who Is Arielle?\n\nI'm Arielle. I live in the countryside, and every day I face a rare condition called Epidermolysis Bullosa that causes painful wounds across my body.\n\nEvery new wound means more pain. Every flare-up requires specialized care that my family cannot afford alone. The dressings, medical visits, medication, nutrition and supplies I need already exceed $90,000.\n\nPlease help me keep fighting. Your donation can give me a night without pain.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/healing.webp|Special dressings and careful wound treatment help reduce Arielle's pain.\n\nWhy Your Help Matters\n\nWithout continued treatment, Arielle may keep suffering intense flare-ups, open wounds and blood loss. Her family cannot keep up with the medical care she needs, and the disease can continue progressing and putting her life at risk.\n\nWith support, Arielle can receive better wound dressings, medical visits, medication and nutrition. Consistent care can reduce her suffering and help a young girl live with greater independence, dignity and hope.\n\nEvery donation, no matter the amount, can be the difference between Arielle having a calmer night or another night of burning pain. She cannot do this alone.\n\nFull Transparency — Monthly Costs\n\nSpecial wound dressings for Epidermolysis Bullosa: $86,800. Medical visits and tests: $3,000. Gastroenterologist visits: $1,000. Dermatologist visits: $750. Supplements, vitamins and medication: $600. Nutritionist visits: $600. Transportation and other expenses: $500. Moisturizers and skin care: $300. Total monthly need: $93,550.\n\nIMAGE:uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/vitamins.webp|Nutrition and supplements are an important part of Arielle's ongoing care.\n\nCampaign Updates\n\nJuly 2026 — Arielle's story went online. The campaign started to spread, but the amount raised is still far from what she needs. Every share and donation brings her closer to full treatment.\n\nJune 2026 — Arielle's condition became worse. New wounds appeared across larger areas of her body, and her dressings had to be changed almost every day. The cost continued rising with medication, visits and supplies.\n\nFebruary 2026 — The family ran out of money to cover medication, household bills and dressing supplies in the same month. Arielle's mother had to stretch every penny.\n\nNovember 2025 — The family filed a legal case requesting proper dressings through the government, but the process remains unresolved. That impasse led to this campaign.\n\nPlease help Arielle receive the care she needs. If donating is not possible, sharing her story can help it reach someone who can.","image_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/1.webp","images":["uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/1.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/2.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/3.webp","uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/4.webp"],"video_player":"arielle","video_url":"uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/arielle-story.mp4","video_poster":"uploads/campaigns/help-arielle/video-poster.jpg","video_label":"Arielle's Story","video_heading":"See Arielle's Real Story","video_description":"Watch Arielle explain the reality of living with painful wounds and why consistent treatment is so urgent.","video_warning":"This video contains real images of Arielle's medical condition.","raised":1005.73,"goal":93550,"category":"children","active":true,"listed":true,"spanish":false,"urgent":true,"organizer":"Lumani Impact","location":"Brazil","words_of_support":[],"donations_count":"34","created_at":"2026-07-01T00:00:00+00:00","stripe_account_id":"bhf","source_url":"https://hopebridgefoundation.live/","currency":"USD"}];
  const SITE_CONFIG = {"scope_id":"bhf","org_name":"Lumani Impact","domain":"camp.lumani-impact.org","site_url":"https://camp.lumani-impact.org","logo_nav":"lumani-impact-logo.png","logo_footer":"lumani-impact-logo.png","logo_icon":"lumani-impact-logo.png","favicon":"lumani-impact-favicon.png","checkout_domain":"https://lumani-impactt.site","checkout_links":{"500": "https://buy.stripe.com/4gMcMZ5sG7Oodu691E0ZW01", "200": "https://buy.stripe.com/3cIbIV7AO5GgfCeelY0ZW02", "150": "https://buy.stripe.com/bJefZbg7k1q0ahU3Hk0ZW03", "100": "https://buy.stripe.com/fZubIV5sG6Kk0Hk2Dg0ZW04", "50": "https://buy.stripe.com/aFadR34oC6Kkdu62Dg0ZW05", "25": "https://buy.stripe.com/dRm9AN7AO8Ss9dQ1zc0ZW06"},"default_checkout_domain":"https://check.lumani-us.org","default_checkout_links":{"500": "https://buy.stripe.com/4gMcMZ5sG7Oodu691E0ZW01", "200": "https://buy.stripe.com/3cIbIV7AO5GgfCeelY0ZW02", "150": "https://buy.stripe.com/bJefZbg7k1q0ahU3Hk0ZW03", "100": "https://buy.stripe.com/fZubIV5sG6Kk0Hk2Dg0ZW04", "50": "https://buy.stripe.com/aFadR34oC6Kkdu62Dg0ZW05", "25": "https://buy.stripe.com/dRm9AN7AO8Ss9dQ1zc0ZW06"}};
  const nativeFetch = window.fetch ? window.fetch.bind(window) : null;

  function cloneRows() { return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(CAMPAIGNS)); }
  function jsonResponse(value, status) {
    return Promise.resolve(new Response(JSON.stringify(value), {
      status: status || 200,
      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}
    }));
  }
  function applyCampaignQuery(rawUrl) {
    const url = new URL(rawUrl, 'https://offline.local');
    let rows = cloneRows();
    const slug = url.searchParams.get('slug');
    const id = url.searchParams.get('id');
    const active = url.searchParams.get('active');
    const listed = url.searchParams.get('listed');
    const excluded = id && id.startsWith('not.in.')
      ? id.replace(/^not\.in\.\(|\)$/g, '').split(',') : [];
    if (slug && slug.startsWith('eq.')) rows = rows.filter(c => String(c.slug) === slug.slice(3));
    if (id && id.startsWith('eq.')) rows = rows.filter(c => String(c.id) === id.slice(3));
    if (excluded.length) rows = rows.filter(c => !excluded.includes(String(c.id)));
    if (active === 'eq.true') rows = rows.filter(c => c.active === true);
    if (listed === 'eq.true') rows = rows.filter(c => c.listed === true);
    const order = url.searchParams.get('order') || '';
    if (order.startsWith('raised.desc')) rows.sort((a,b) => Number(b.raised||0)-Number(a.raised||0));
    if (order.startsWith('created_at.desc')) rows.sort((a,b) => String(b.created_at||'').localeCompare(String(a.created_at||'')));
    return rows;
  }

  window.OFFLINE_MODE = true;
  window.OFFLINE_CAMPAIGNS = CAMPAIGNS;
  window.fetch = function(input, init) {
    const raw = typeof input === 'string' ? input : (input && input.url) || '';
    const method = (init && init.method || 'GET').toUpperCase();
    try { const live = new URL(raw, window.location.href); if (live.origin === 'https://help-ross.vercel.app' && live.pathname === '/api/meta-events' && nativeFetch) return nativeFetch(input, init); } catch (_) {}
    if (raw.includes('/rest/v1/campaigns')) {
      if (method !== 'GET')
        return jsonResponse({error:'This static site does not support writes.'}, 405);
      return jsonResponse(applyCampaignQuery(raw));
    }
    if (raw.includes('/api/site-config.php')) return jsonResponse(SITE_CONFIG);
    if (raw.includes('api.web3forms.com/submit') && method === 'POST')
      return jsonResponse({success:false,error:'Messaging is unavailable.'}, 503);
    if (raw.includes('/storage/v1/object/') && method === 'POST')
      return jsonResponse({error:'This static site does not support writes.'}, 405);
    if (raw.includes('/api/') || raw.includes('/storage/v1/object/'))
      return jsonResponse({offline:true,error:'Operacao indisponivel na copia local.'}, 503);
    if (nativeFetch) return nativeFetch(input, init);
    return Promise.reject(new Error('Fetch indisponivel nesta copia local.'));
  };

  if (typeof document !== 'undefined') {
    document.addEventListener('click', function(event) {
      const target = event.target;
      if (!document.getElementById('peSubmitBtn')) return;
      const trigger = target && target.closest ? target.closest('.nav-trigger') : null;
      if (trigger) {
        event.stopPropagation();
        const item = trigger.closest('.nav-item');
        const wasOpen = item && item.classList.contains('open');
        document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('open'));
        if (item && !wasOpen) item.classList.add('open');
      } else if (!(target && target.closest && target.closest('.nav-item'))) {
        document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('open'));
      }
    }, true);
  }
})();
